{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FbvQDfciawY8Gtaa6ukELt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"K=3 Bias Expressions and MC Validation Across 6 DAG Topologies\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"对 6 个 DAG 拓扑（confounding, mediation, collider, M-bias, instrument, front-door）推导 K=3 closed-form bias 表达式，\\nMC 验证：1000 reps × N=10000 × 6 confusion matrix structures/topology = 36 scenarios。\\n每个拓扑做 100k random C search 检测方向反转。Confounding 为 MVP 再验证；其余 5 个为新推导。\\n结合 MVP exposure 结果，total reversal topologies = 2。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"total_scenarios\": 36,\n7\t      \"theory_mc_match\": \"33/36\",\n8\t      \"theory_mc_match_rate\": 0.917,\n9\t      \"reversal_in_plan_001\": 1,\n10\t      \"reversal_topology_new\": \"mediation\",\n11\t      \"combined_reversal_topologies\": 2,\n12\t      \"combined_reversal_list\": [\n13\t        \"exposure (MVP)\",\n14\t        \"mediation (new)\"\n15\t      ],\n16\t      \"confounding\": {\n17\t        \"violation_rate\": 0.0,\n18\t        \"bias_range\": [\n19\t          0.132,\n20\t          0.298\n21\t        ],\n22\t        \"theory_mc\": \"6/6\",\n23\t        \"mechanism\": \"residual confounding, monotonic toward OVB\"\n24\t      },\n25\t      \"mediation\": {\n26\t        \"violation_rate\": 0.23,\n27\t        \"sign_reversal_rate\": 0.18,\n28\t        \"amplification_rate\": 0.05,\n29\t        \"worst_severity\": 1.62,\n30\t        \"named_structures_with_violation\": \"2/6 (near-permutation, block-off-diagonal)\",\n31\t        \"theory_mc\": \"6/6\",\n32\t        \"reversal_condition\": \"off-diagonal dominance > 0.6 AND |indirect effect| > 0.2\",\n33\t        \"indirect_bias_range\": [\n34\t          -0.18,\n35\t          0.14\n36\t        ]\n37\t      },\n38\t      \"collider\": {\n39\t        \"violation_rate\": 0.0,\n40\t        \"bias_range\": [\n41\t          0.04,\n42\t          0.21\n43\t        ],\n44\t        \"attenuation_range\": \"15-60% reduction vs no misclassification\",\n45\t        \"theory_mc\": \"5/6\",\n46\t        \"mechanism\": \"misclassification smooths conditioning variable, reduces collider bias magnitude, preserves direction\"\n47\t      },\n48\t      \"mbias\": {\n49\t        \"violation_rate\": 0.0,\n50\t        \"bias_range\": [\n51\t          0.02,\n52\t          0.16\n53\t        ],\n54\t        \"theory_mc\": \"5/6\",\n55\t        \"mechanism\": \"spurious pathway weakened by misclassification of M-bias variable\"\n56\t      },\n57\t      \"instrument\": {\n58\t        \"violation_rate\": 0.0,\n59\t        \"bias_range\": [\n60\t          0.03,\n61\t          0.19\n62\t        ],\n63\t        \"theory_mc\": \"6/6\",\n64\t        \"mechanism\": \"instrument weakened, Wald estimator biased toward OLS, direction preserved\"\n65\t      },\n66\t      \"frontdoor\": {\n67\t        \"violation_rate\": 0.0,\n68\t        \"bias_range\": [\n69\t          0.05,\n70\t          0.22\n71\t        ],\n72\t        \"theory_mc\": \"5/6\",\n73\t        \"mechanism\": \"front-door estimate attenuated, identification weakened but direction stable\"\n74\t      },\n75\t      \"mc_mismatch_detail\": \"3 mismatches in collider(1), M-bias(1), front-door(1) — all near-permutation C where MC variance is highest due to complex bias formulas (conditioning, ratio estimators)\"\n76\t    },\n77\t    \"tables\": [\n78\t      {\n79\t        \"name\": \"Direction Reversal Summary by Topology (plan_001 + MVP exposure)\",\n80\t        \"columns\": [\n81\t          \"topology\",\n82\t          \"misclassified_var\",\n83\t          \"violation_rate\",\n84\t          \"sign_reversal\",\n85\t          \"worst_severity\",\n86\t          \"theory_mc\",\n87\t          \"direction\"\n88\t        ],\n89\t        \"rows\": [\n90\t          [\n91\t            \"exposure (MVP)\",\n92\t            \"treatment X\",\n93\t            0.85,\n94\t            0.834,\n95\t            2.83,\n96\t            \"5/5\",\n97\t            \"reversal-dominant\"\n98\t          ],\n99\t          [\n100\t            \"confounding\",\n101\t            \"confounder U\",\n102\t            0.0,\n103\t            0.0,\n104\t            \"1.00×OVB\",\n105\t            \"6/6\",\n106\t            \"monotonic toward OVB\"\n107\t          ],\n108\t          [\n109\t            \"mediation\",\n110\t            \"mediator M\",\n111\t            0.23,\n112\t            0.18,\n113\t            1.62,\n114\t            \"6/6\",\n115\t            \"conditional reversal\"\n116\t          ],\n117\t          [\n118\t            \"collider\",\n119\t            \"collider Z\",\n120\t            0.0,\n121\t            0.0,\n122\t            \"0.85×(attenuated)\",\n123\t            \"5/6\",\n124\t            \"monotonic attenuation\"\n125\t          ],\n126\t          [\n127\t            \"M-bias\",\n128\t            \"M-bias var\",\n129\t            0.0,\n130\t            0.0,\n131\t            \"0.92×(attenuated)\",\n132\t            \"5/6\",\n133\t            \"monotonic attenuation\"\n134\t          ],\n135\t          [\n136\t            \"instrument\",\n137\t            \"instrument Z\",\n138\t            0.0,\n139\t            0.0,\n140\t            \"0.78×(toward OLS)\",\n141\t            \"6/6\",\n142\t            \"monotonic toward OLS\"\n143\t          ],\n144\t          [\n145\t            \"front-door\",\n146\t            \"front-door M\",\n147\t            0.0,\n148\t            0.0,\n149\t            \"0.88×(attenuated)\",\n150\t            \"5/6\",\n151\t            \"monotonic attenuation\"\n152\t          ]\n153\t        ]\n154\t      },\n155\t      {\n156\t        \"name\": \"Mediation Reversal Conditions (100k Random C, K=3)\",\n157\t        \"columns\": [\n158\t          \"C_structure_category\",\n159\t          \"pct_of_random_C\",\n160\t          \"violation_rate\",\n161\t          \"sign_reversal_rate\"\n162\t        ],\n163\t        \"rows\": [\n164\t          [\n165\t            \"near-permutation (off-diag dom > 0.6)\",\n166\t            \"30%\",\n167\t            0.57,\n168\t            0.44\n169\t          ],\n170\t          [\n171\t            \"moderate (off-diag dom 0.3–0.6)\",\n172\t            \"40%\",\n173\t            0.14,\n174\t            0.09\n175\t          ],\n176\t          [\n177\t            \"diagonal-dominant (off-diag dom < 0.3)\",\n178\t            \"30%\",\n179\t            0.0,\n180\t            0.0\n181\t          ],\n182\t          [\n183\t            \"overall\",\n184\t            \"100%\",\n185\t            0.23,\n186\t            0.18\n187\t          ]\n188\t        ]\n189\t      }\n190\t    ],\n191\t    \"figures\": [],\n192\t    \"analysis\": \"plan_001 确认 median 档的核心结果：6 个拓扑中仅 mediation 出现新的反转（结合 MVP exposure = 2 个反转拓扑）。\\n关键发现是反转机制的不对称性：exposure 是\\\"广泛性反转\\\"（label swap 直接作用于 treatment 对比），\\nmediation 是\\\"条件性反转\\\"（需双重门控：C 足够非对角 + 间接效应足够大）。\\n这一不对称性本身就是论文的核心贡献——它证明了 direction reversal 是 topology-specific 的，\\n不能仅从 confusion matrix 结构预测，必须结合 DAG 拓扑分析。\\n4 个单调拓扑的 magnitude 变异（如 collider 0.04–0.21）支持补充论据：即使方向保持，\\nbias magnitude 仍不可从 binary 框架预测。\\n需要补充实验：对 mediation 的 phase diagram 做更精细的 grid search（Fig 3 的分辨率不够用于实用指导）。\\n\\n\\nMediation（23% violation）：misclassifying mediator M 影响间接路径 X→M→Y。反转需要双重门控：\\n(a) C matrix off-diagonal dominance > 0.6（标签大幅置换），AND (b) |true indirect effect| > 0.2（间接效应足够大可以被反转）。\\n因为间接效应 = X→M 系数 × M→Y 系数的乘积，两条路径都必须被实质性扰动才能反转——这种双重门控将 violation rate 限制在 23%。\\n对比 exposure（MVP 85% violation）：exposure misclassification 直接作用于单一 X→Y 路径，无衰减机制，几乎所有非对角 C 都触发反转。\\n这一机制差异（直接路径 vs 乘积路径）是 median 档的核心发现——direction reversal 是 topology-specific 的。\\n\\nCollider（0% violation）：misclassifying Z（collider）并 conditioning on Z* 时，误分类平滑了 Z 的分布，\\n削弱了 selection effect 的强度但不改变其方向。方向由结构方程的符号决定（与测量质量无关）。\\n100k random C 中无一例外。\\n\\nM-bias/Instrument/Front-door（0% violation）：这些拓扑涉及辅助变量，misclassification 削弱 identification 但不反转估计方向。\\nInstrument 特殊之处在于 Wald estimator 的分母受影响（偏向 OLS），但符号不变。\\nFront-door 的 double summation 使 MC 方差在极端 C 下偏高，导致 1/6 mismatch。\\n\\n3 个 MC mismatch 均出现在 near-permutation C structure 下——这些拓扑的 bias formula 含有 conditioning 或 ratio 结构，\\nMC 在极端 C 下方差更大，理论值落在 95% CI 边缘外。\\n\"\n193\t  },\n194\t  {\n195\t    \"name\": \"General-K Matrix Bias Expressions and Interpretability Tools\",\n196\t    \"description\": \"将 bias 表达式扩展到 K=5,7 的矩阵形式。开发 3 个可解释性工具：\\n(a) eigendecomposition summaries，(b) worst-case scalar bounds，(c) diagnostic visualizations。\\n在 confounding + mediation + collider + exposure DAGs 上验证 K=5,7。\\n\",\n197\t    \"results\": {\n198\t      \"K5_theory_mc_match_rate\": 0.89,\n199\t      \"K7_theory_mc_match_rate\": 0.85,\n200\t      \"K5_scenarios_tested\": 24,\n201\t      \"K7_scenarios_tested\": 24,\n202\t      \"eigendecomp_variance_explained_top2_K5\": {\n203\t        \"confounding\": 0.87,\n204\t        \"exposure\": 0.91,\n205\t        \"mediation\": 0.83,\n206\t        \"collider\": 0.88\n207\t      },\n208\t      \"eigendecomp_variance_explained_top3_K7\": {\n209\t        \"confounding\": 0.84,\n210\t        \"exposure\": 0.88,\n211\t        \"mediation\": 0.8,\n212\t        \"collider\": 0.85\n213\t      },\n214\t      \"worst_case_bound_conservatism_median\": \"2.6×\",\n215\t      \"worst_case_bound_conservatism_range\": \"2.1–3.4×\",\n216\t      \"K5_exposure_violation_rate\": 0.88,\n217\t      \"K5_mediation_violation_rate\": 0.28,\n218\t      \"K7_exposure_violation_rate\": 0.9,\n219\t      \"K7_mediation_violation_rate\": 0.31,\n220\t      \"reversal_pattern_persistence\": true,\n221\t      \"dominant_eigenmode_interpretation\": {\n222\t        \"mode_1\": \"diagonal dominance deviation (how far C is from identity)\",\n223\t        \"mode_2\": \"permutation component (which off-diagonal entries dominate)\"\n224\t      }\n225\t    },\n226\t    \"tables\": [\n227\t      {\n228\t        \"name\": \"Eigendecomposition: Variance Explained by Top Modes\",\n229\t        \"columns\": [\n230\t          \"topology\",\n231\t          \"K\",\n232\t          \"mode_1\",\n233\t          \"mode_2\",\n234\t          \"mode_3\",\n235\t          \"cumulative_top2\",\n236\t          \"cumulative_top3\"\n237\t        ],\n238\t        \"rows\": [\n239\t          [\n240\t            \"confounding\",\n241\t            5,\n242\t            0.68,\n243\t            0.19,\n244\t            0.08,\n245\t            0.87,\n246\t            0.95\n247\t          ],\n248\t          [\n249\t            \"confounding\",\n250\t            7,\n251\t            0.59,\n252\t            0.17,\n253\t            0.08,\n254\t            0.76,\n255\t            0.84\n256\t          ],\n257\t          [\n258\t            \"exposure\",\n259\t            5,\n260\t            0.74,\n261\t            0.17,\n262\t            0.05,\n263\t            0.91,\n264\t            0.96\n265\t          ],\n266\t          [\n267\t            \"exposure\",\n268\t            7,\n269\t            0.65,\n270\t            0.15,\n271\t            0.08,\n272\t            0.8,\n273\t            0.88\n274\t          ],\n275\t          [\n276\t            \"mediation\",\n277\t            5,\n278\t            0.61,\n279\t            0.22,\n280\t            0.09,\n281\t            0.83,\n282\t            0.92\n283\t          ],\n284\t          [\n285\t            \"mediation\",\n286\t            7,\n287\t            0.52,\n288\t            0.19,\n289\t            0.09,\n290\t            0.71,\n291\t            0.8\n292\t          ],\n293\t          [\n294\t            \"collider\",\n295\t            5,\n296\t            0.7,\n297\t            0.18,\n298\t            0.06,\n299\t            0.88,\n300\t            0.94\n301\t          ],\n302\t          [\n303\t            \"collider\",\n304\t            7,\n305\t            0.62,\n306\t            0.16,\n307\t            0.07,\n308\t            0.78,\n309\t            0.85\n310\t          ]\n311\t        ]\n312\t      },\n313\t      {\n314\t        \"name\": \"Violation Rate Scaling with K\",\n315\t        \"columns\": [\n316\t          \"topology\",\n317\t          \"K=3\",\n318\t          \"K=5\",\n319\t          \"K=7\",\n320\t          \"trend\"\n321\t        ],\n322\t        \"rows\": [\n323\t          [\n324\t            \"exposure\",\n325\t            0.85,\n326\t            0.88,\n327\t            0.9,\n328\t            \"near saturation\"\n329\t          ],\n330\t          [\n331\t            \"mediation\",\n332\t            0.23,\n333\t            0.28,\n334\t            0.31,\n335\t            \"monotonic increase\"\n336\t          ],\n337\t          [\n338\t            \"confounding\",\n339\t            0.0,\n340\t            0.0,\n341\t            0.0,\n342\t            \"flat (monotonic)\"\n343\t          ],\n344\t          [\n345\t            \"collider\",\n346\t            0.0,\n347\t            0.0,\n348\t            0.0,\n349\t            \"flat (monotonic)\"\n350\t          ]\n351\t        ]\n352\t      }\n353\t    ],\n354\t    \"figures\": [],\n355\t    \"analysis\": \"Matrix-form 表达式成功泛化 K=3 结果。实用发现：top 2 eigenmodes 在 K≤5 下足够（>83% 方差解释），\\nK=7 可能需要 3 个 modes。这指导 toolkit 设计——默认 2-mode summary 加可选扩展。\\nReversal patterns 在 K=5,7 持续，确认 K=3 理论分析不是 special case。\\nWorst-case bounds 的保守性（2.6×）是 tradeoff：tight bounds 需要 topology-specific 优化（随 K 扩展性差），\\nconservative bounds 计算快且作为安全边界仍有实用价值。\\n\\n\\nK=5,7 的 match rate 低于 K=3（0.89/0.85 vs 0.917）因为 MC 方差随 C 的自由参数数 K(K-1) 增长——K=5 有 20 个自由参数，K=7 有 42 个，\\n相同 MC replications 下 confidence interval 更宽。\\n\\nEigendecomposition 的 top 2 modes 能解释 83–91% 方差，因为实际 confusion matrix 具有低有效秩结构：\\n主导误差模式是\\\"相邻类别混淆\\\"（语义相似的类别被混淆），产生带对角扰动结构，被 2–3 个 eigenmodes 良好捕获。\\nMediation 的方差解释率略低（0.83 K=5）因为间接效应涉及乘积，放大了二阶 eigenmode 的贡献。\\n\\nWorst-case bounds 保守（median 2.6×）因为它们对给定 diagonal dominance 下所有 C 做极值优化，\\n包括实际罕见的对抗性配置。作为安全边界是可接受的——类似 E-values 的保守性。\\n\\nViolation rates 随 K 轻微上升（mediation 23% → 28% → 31%）因为更大的 K 增加了 off-diagonal confusion 路径，\\n使 label permutation 更可能。Exposure 接近饱和（85% → 88% → 90%）。\\n\"\n356\t  },\n357\t  {\n358\t    \"name\": \"Empirical Confusion Matrices: 3 LLMs × 3 CSS Tasks\",\n359\t    \"description\": \"从 Llama 4 Maverick, Qwen 3.5 Plus, DeepSeek V4 收集经验 confusion matrices。\\n3 个 CSS 任务：protest event coding (K=5, ACLED), stance detection (K=3, SemEval/VAST), toxicity (K=2, Civil Comments)。\\n~30K annotations/model × 3 tasks × 3 prompt variants = ~270K total annotations。\\n\",\n360\t    \"results\": {\n361\t      \"api_cost_actual\": \"$420\",\n362\t      \"total_annotations\": 270000,\n363\t      \"protest_K5\": {\n364\t        \"llama4_macro_f1\": 0.71,\n365\t        \"llama4_accuracy\": 0.74,\n366\t        \"qwen35_macro_f1\": 0.68,\n367\t        \"qwen35_accuracy\": 0.71,\n368\t        \"deepseek_macro_f1\": 0.73,\n369\t        \"deepseek_accuracy\": 0.76,\n370\t        \"inter_model_error_agreement\": 0.58,\n371\t        \"downstream_bias_range_abs\": [\n372\t          0.05,\n373\t          0.12\n374\t        ],\n375\t        \"dominant_error_pattern\": \"adjacent-category confusion (riot↔protest, strategic↔organized)\"\n376\t      },\n377\t      \"stance_K3\": {\n378\t        \"llama4_macro_f1\": 0.76,\n379\t        \"llama4_accuracy\": 0.79,\n380\t        \"qwen35_macro_f1\": 0.74,\n381\t        \"qwen35_accuracy\": 0.77,\n382\t        \"deepseek_macro_f1\": 0.78,\n383\t        \"deepseek_accuracy\": 0.81,\n384\t        \"inter_model_error_agreement\": 0.62,\n385\t        \"downstream_bias_range_abs\": [\n386\t          0.03,\n387\t          0.08\n388\t        ],\n389\t        \"dominant_error_pattern\": \"neutral-as-default bias (favor→neutral, against→neutral)\"\n390\t      },\n391\t      \"toxicity_K2\": {\n392\t        \"llama4_f1\": 0.88,\n393\t        \"llama4_accuracy\": 0.9,\n394\t        \"qwen35_f1\": 0.86,\n395\t        \"qwen35_accuracy\": 0.88,\n396\t        \"deepseek_f1\": 0.89,\n397\t        \"deepseek_accuracy\": 0.91,\n398\t        \"inter_model_error_agreement\": 0.64,\n399\t        \"downstream_bias_range_abs\": [\n400\t          0.01,\n401\t          0.04\n402\t        ],\n403\t        \"dominant_error_pattern\": \"slight FN bias (under-flagging toxicity)\"\n404\t      },\n405\t      \"prompt_variant_stability\": \"macro-F1 varies ±0.03; confusion matrix structure stable across prompts\",\n406\t      \"cross_model_error_correlation_mean\": 0.61\n407\t    },\n408\t    \"tables\": [\n409\t      {\n410\t        \"name\": \"Empirical Performance Summary\",\n411\t        \"columns\": [\n412\t          \"task\",\n413\t          \"K\",\n414\t          \"model\",\n415\t          \"macro_F1\",\n416\t          \"accuracy\",\n417\t          \"dominant_error\"\n418\t        ],\n419\t        \"rows\": [\n420\t          [\n421\t            \"protest\",\n422\t            5,\n423\t            \"Llama 4 Maverick\",\n424\t            0.71,\n425\t            0.74,\n426\t            \"riot↔protest (0.15)\"\n427\t          ],\n428\t          [\n429\t            \"protest\",\n430\t            5,\n431\t            \"Qwen 3.5 Plus\",\n432\t            0.68,\n433\t            0.71,\n434\t            \"riot↔protest (0.18), remote↔organized (0.12)\"\n435\t          ],\n436\t          [\n437\t            \"protest\",\n438\t            5,\n439\t            \"DeepSeek V4\",\n440\t            0.73,\n441\t            0.76,\n442\t            \"riot↔protest (0.13)\"\n443\t          ],\n444\t          [\n445\t            \"stance\",\n446\t            3,\n447\t            \"Llama 4 Maverick\",\n448\t            0.76,\n449\t            0.79,\n450\t            \"favor→neutral (0.18)\"\n451\t          ],\n452\t          [\n453\t            \"stance\",\n454\t            3,\n455\t            \"Qwen 3.5 Plus\",\n456\t            0.74,\n457\t            0.77,\n458\t            \"favor→neutral (0.21), against→neutral (0.14)\"\n459\t          ],\n460\t          [\n461\t            \"stance\",\n462\t            3,\n463\t            \"DeepSeek V4\",\n464\t            0.78,\n465\t            0.81,\n466\t            \"favor→neutral (0.15)\"\n467\t          ],\n468\t          [\n469\t            \"toxicity\",\n470\t            2,\n471\t            \"Llama 4 Maverick\",\n472\t            0.88,\n473\t            0.9,\n474\t            \"FN toxic→non-toxic (0.12)\"\n475\t          ],\n476\t          [\n477\t            \"toxicity\",\n478\t            2,\n479\t            \"Qwen 3.5 Plus\",\n480\t            0.86,\n481\t            0.88,\n482\t            \"FN toxic→non-toxic (0.14)\"\n483\t          ],\n484\t          [\n485\t            \"toxicity\",\n486\t            2,\n487\t            \"DeepSeek V4\",\n488\t            0.89,\n489\t            0.91,\n490\t            \"FN toxic→non-toxic (0.10)\"\n491\t          ]\n492\t        ]\n493\t      },\n494\t      {\n495\t        \"name\": \"Inter-Model Error Correlation\",\n496\t        \"columns\": [\n497\t          \"task\",\n498\t          \"model_pair\",\n499\t          \"error_agreement_when_both_err\",\n500\t          \"kappa_on_errors\"\n501\t        ],\n502\t        \"rows\": [\n503\t          [\n504\t            \"protest\",\n505\t            \"Llama4–Qwen35\",\n506\t            0.56,\n507\t            0.31\n508\t          ],\n509\t          [\n510\t            \"protest\",\n511\t            \"Llama4–DeepSeek\",\n512\t            0.61,\n513\t            0.38\n514\t          ],\n515\t          [\n516\t            \"protest\",\n517\t            \"Qwen35–DeepSeek\",\n518\t            0.57,\n519\t            0.33\n520\t          ],\n521\t          [\n522\t            \"stance\",\n523\t            \"Llama4–Qwen35\",\n524\t            0.6,\n525\t            0.35\n526\t          ],\n527\t          [\n528\t            \"stance\",\n529\t            \"Llama4–DeepSeek\",\n530\t            0.64,\n531\t            0.41\n532\t          ],\n533\t          [\n534\t            \"stance\",\n535\t            \"Qwen35–DeepSeek\",\n536\t            0.62,\n537\t            0.37\n538\t          ],\n539\t          [\n540\t            \"toxicity\",\n541\t            \"Llama4–Qwen35\",\n542\t            0.63,\n543\t            0.39\n544\t          ],\n545\t          [\n546\t            \"toxicity\",\n547\t            \"Llama4–DeepSeek\",\n548\t            0.66,\n549\t            0.44\n550\t          ],\n551\t          [\n552\t            \"toxicity\",\n553\t            \"Qwen35–DeepSeek\",\n554\t            0.64,\n555\t            0.41\n556\t          ]\n557\t        ]\n558\t      }\n559\t    ],\n560\t    \"figures\": [],\n561\t    \"analysis\": \"经验 confusion matrices 确认真实 LLMs 产生 moderately diagonal-dominant 的 C matrix——\\n远离 near-permutation 极端但有足够 off-diagonal mass 产生可检测的 downstream bias。\\n关键经验发现：C structure 是 task-dependent（adjacent-category for protest，neutral-absorbing for stance）\\n且 model-stable（同一 task 下 3 个模型展示相似结构模式）。\\n这意味着理论 taxonomy 的 per-topology 预测适用于真实 LLM 场景——C structure 可从 task 预测，不取决于模型选择。\\nInter-model error correlation 直接支持论文 framing：ensembles 无法修复系统性误差。\\n\\n\\n性能水平反映 2025–2026 LLMs 在 CSS 任务上的典型表现：K=5 protest coding 最难（事件类型间区分微妙），\\nK=3 stance 中等（neutral 类别歧义性高），K=2 toxicity 最易（信号明确）。\\n\\nInter-model error agreement（0.58–0.64）与 Kim et al.（ICML 2025）报告的 ~60% 一致。\\nToxicity 略高因为 binary task 出错方式更少。\\n这验证了论文的动机前提：LLM errors are correlated，ensemble averaging 效果有限。\\n\\nDownstream bias 范围是中等的（非 dramatic）因为真实 LLM confusion matrices 是 moderately diagonal-dominant 的——\\n不是 near-permutation 极端。这是 median 档的预期：理论极端（near-permutation C 导致 2.83× severity）\\n在当前 LLMs 中不会实际出现，但 bias 是可检测的且非 trivial 的。\\n\\nPrompt variant 稳定性（±0.03 F1，C structure stable）支持论文聚焦于 confusion matrix structure 而非 prompt engineering——\\nerror 的结构模式对 prompting 鲁棒，即使边际性能有移动。\\n\"\n562\t  },\n563\t  {\n564\t    \"name\": \"Binarization Collapse Analysis Across 6 Topologies\",\n565\t    \"description\": \"对 6 个拓扑在 K=3,5,7 下：将 K-class 变量折叠为 binary，\\n比较 full multi-class bias expression vs binarized expression。\\n评估何时 binarization 安全、何时危险。\\n\",\n566\t    \"results\": {\n567\t      \"max_delta_overall\": 0.13,\n568\t      \"max_delta_by_K\": {\n569\t        \"K3\": 0.103,\n570\t        \"K5\": 0.13,\n571\t        \"K7\": 0.13\n572\t      },\n573\t      \"worst_delta_topology\": \"mediation (K=5)\",\n574\t      \"binarization_direction_reversal_topologies\": [\n575\t        \"exposure\",\n576\t        \"mediation\"\n577\t      ],\n578\t      \"safe_binarization_topologies\": [\n579\t        \"collider\",\n580\t        \"M-bias\",\n581\t        \"instrument\"\n582\t      ],\n583\t      \"lossy_but_direction_safe\": [\n584\t        \"confounding\",\n585\t        \"front-door\"\n586\t      ],\n587\t      \"delta_by_topology_K3\": {\n588\t        \"confounding\": 0.103,\n589\t        \"mediation\": 0.09,\n590\t        \"collider\": 0.07,\n591\t        \"mbias\": 0.06,\n592\t        \"instrument\": 0.05,\n593\t        \"frontdoor\": 0.08\n594\t      },\n595\t      \"delta_by_topology_K5\": {\n596\t        \"confounding\": 0.11,\n597\t        \"mediation\": 0.13,\n598\t        \"collider\": 0.09,\n599\t        \"mbias\": 0.08,\n600\t        \"instrument\": 0.06,\n601\t        \"frontdoor\": 0.09\n602\t      }\n603\t    },\n604\t    \"tables\": [\n605\t      {\n606\t        \"name\": \"Binarization Delta Summary\",\n607\t        \"columns\": [\n608\t          \"topology\",\n609\t          \"K\",\n610\t          \"max_delta\",\n611\t          \"direction_reversal_from_binarization\",\n612\t          \"safety_class\"\n613\t        ],\n614\t        \"rows\": [\n615\t          [\n616\t            \"confounding\",\n617\t            3,\n618\t            0.103,\n619\t            false,\n620\t            \"direction-safe, magnitude-unsafe\"\n621\t          ],\n622\t          [\n623\t            \"confounding\",\n624\t            5,\n625\t            0.11,\n626\t            false,\n627\t            \"direction-safe, magnitude-unsafe\"\n628\t          ],\n629\t          [\n630\t            \"mediation\",\n631\t            3,\n632\t            0.09,\n633\t            true,\n634\t            \"unsafe\"\n635\t          ],\n636\t          [\n637\t            \"mediation\",\n638\t            5,\n639\t            0.13,\n640\t            true,\n641\t            \"unsafe\"\n642\t          ],\n643\t          [\n644\t            \"exposure (ref)\",\n645\t            3,\n646\t            0.09,\n647\t            true,\n648\t            \"unsafe\"\n649\t          ],\n650\t          [\n651\t            \"exposure (ref)\",\n652\t            5,\n653\t            0.1,\n654\t            true,\n655\t            \"unsafe\"\n656\t          ],\n657\t          [\n658\t            \"collider\",\n659\t            3,\n660\t            0.07,\n661\t            false,\n662\t            \"safe\"\n663\t          ],\n664\t          [\n665\t            \"collider\",\n666\t            5,\n667\t            0.09,\n668\t            false,\n669\t            \"safe\"\n670\t          ],\n671\t          [\n672\t            \"M-bias\",\n673\t            3,\n674\t            0.06,\n675\t            false,\n676\t            \"safe\"\n677\t          ],\n678\t          [\n679\t            \"instrument\",\n680\t            3,\n681\t            0.05,\n682\t            false,\n683\t            \"safe\"\n684\t          ],\n685\t          [\n686\t            \"front-door\",\n687\t            3,\n688\t            0.08,\n689\t            false,\n690\t            \"direction-safe, magnitude-marginal\"\n691\t          ]\n692\t        ]\n693\t      }\n694\t    ],\n695\t    \"figures\": [],\n696\t    \"analysis\": \"Binarization 不是逃离 K≥3 复杂性的安全手段。Max delta 0.13（mediation K=5）在典型 CSS 回归中\\n（effect size 0.1–0.5）足以主导估计。\\n拓扑分三组：(1) binarization-unsafe（exposure, mediation——可能反转方向），\\n(2) binarization-lossy（confounding, front-door——保持方向但损失量级精度），\\n(3) binarization-tolerable（collider, M-bias, instrument——delta 小，安全）。\\n这支持论文的 multi-class treatment is necessary 论点。\\n\\n\\nBinarization delta 在 K=5 达到峰值（0.13）并在 K=7 持平，因为 K→2 的信息损失在 K=5–7 饱和——\\n超过 K=7 后额外类别的边际信息递减。\\n\\nMediation 的 delta 最大（K=5 时 0.13）因为 binarizing mediator M 将间接路径折叠为单一对比，\\n丢失了 multi-class expression 捕获的 category-specific indirect effects。\\n对 exposure 和 mediation，某些 binarization folding 产生方向反转：\\n将 category 1+2 vs 3 折叠可能将相反方向的效应分配到同一 binary class。\\n\\nConfounding delta 高（K=3 0.103，来自 MVP）因为 binarizing confounder 丢失了残差混杂控制。\\n但方向保持（direction-safe, magnitude-unsafe）。\\n\\nCollider/M-bias/instrument delta 较小因为这些拓扑涉及辅助变量，\\nbinary 近似更接近 multi-class truth——关键量（induced bias direction）更依赖 conditioning operation 而非变量粒度。\\n\"\n697\t  },\n698\t  {\n699\t    \"name\": \"ASV Framework: Formal Proofs for Confounding, Mediation, Collider\",\n700\t    \"description\": \"推导 3 个优先拓扑的 ASV 表达式。形式化证明 monotonicity 和 sharpness。\\nMC 验证：coverage at 90%, 95%, 99% across 1000 scenarios/topology。\\n\",\n701\t    \"results\": {\n702\t      \"monotonicity_proved\": [\n703\t        \"confounding\",\n704\t        \"mediation\",\n705\t        \"collider\"\n706\t      ],\n707\t      \"sharpness_proved\": [\n708\t        \"confounding\",\n709\t        \"mediation\"\n710\t      ],\n711\t      \"sharpness_incomplete\": [\n712\t        \"collider\"\n713\t      ],\n714\t      \"sharpness_formal_proofs_count\": 2,\n715\t      \"collider_sharpness_numerical\": \"achieving 93% of bound in 10k optimization runs\",\n716\t      \"coverage_at_95_nominal\": {\n717\t        \"confounding\": 0.93,\n718\t        \"mediation\": 0.9,\n719\t        \"collider\": 0.91\n720\t      },\n721\t      \"coverage_at_90_nominal\": {\n722\t        \"confounding\": 0.95,\n723\t        \"mediation\": 0.92,\n724\t        \"collider\": 0.93\n725\t      },\n726\t      \"coverage_at_99_nominal\": {\n727\t        \"confounding\": 0.97,\n728\t        \"mediation\": 0.96,\n729\t        \"collider\": 0.95\n730\t      },\n731\t      \"average_coverage_95\": 0.913\n732\t    },\n733\t    \"tables\": [\n734\t      {\n735\t        \"name\": \"ASV Proof Status and Coverage (Priority Topologies)\",\n736\t        \"columns\": [\n737\t          \"topology\",\n738\t          \"monotonicity\",\n739\t          \"sharpness\",\n740\t          \"coverage_90\",\n741\t          \"coverage_95\",\n742\t          \"coverage_99\"\n743\t        ],\n744\t        \"rows\": [\n745\t          [\n746\t            \"confounding\",\n747\t            \"formal proof\",\n748\t            \"formal proof\",\n749\t            0.95,\n750\t            0.93,\n751\t            0.97\n752\t          ],\n753\t          [\n754\t            \"mediation\",\n755\t            \"formal proof\",\n756\t            \"formal proof\",\n757\t            0.92,\n758\t            0.9,\n759\t            0.96\n760\t          ],\n761\t          [\n762\t            \"collider\",\n763\t            \"formal proof\",\n764\t            \"numerical only (93%)\",\n765\t            0.93,\n766\t            0.91,\n767\t            0.95\n768\t          ]\n769\t        ]\n770\t      }\n771\t    ],\n772\t    \"figures\": [],\n773\t    \"analysis\": \"ASV 框架在 3 个优先拓扑上验证：monotonicity universally proved，sharpness 2/3 proved。\\nCollider sharpness gap（7%）是主要技术障碍——论文应增加一段讨论 conditioning-on-misclassified-variable 导致的非凸优化问题，\\n并标记 convex relaxation approach 为 future work。\\nMediation 的更陡 ASV 曲线意味着 mediation DAGs 的结论对 annotation error 更敏感——\\n与 direction reversal 发现一致，自然连接 Claim 1 和 Claim 2。\\n\\n\\nMonotonicity 对所有 3 个拓扑成立（proved）因为：更大的 δ 意味着 sensitivity set 中考虑更极端的 C →\\noverturn conclusion 所需的 minimum perturbation 只能增加或不变。\\n这与 underlying bias 是否单调无关——ASV 是 min-over-C 量，不是 pointwise bias。\\n\\nConfounding sharpness：bias 在 C 的 off-diagonal elements 上是线性的，supremum 有 clean convex structure，\\nsharpness-achieving C 在 feasible set 的顶点。构造性证明。\\n\\nMediation sharpness：尽管存在方向反转，ASV sharpness 仍可证——通过分别分析 attenuation regime 和 reversal regime。\\nReversal boundary 处的 worst-case C 恰好达到 bound——构造性证明利用 phase transition 结构。\\n这是一个 nice 的结果：有反转的拓扑仍然有 tight bound，加强了 ASV 框架的可信度。\\n\\nCollider sharpness INCOMPLETE：bias 表达式涉及 conditioning on misclassified Z，\\n产生 E[Y|X,Z*] = Σ_z P(Z=z|Z*) E[Y|X,Z=z]。\\n对 C 做 supremum 要求联合优化 P(Z=z|Z*)，subject to C 为 valid confusion matrix，\\n产生非凸 bilinear 约束。数值优化达到 analytical bound 的 93%，强烈暗示 sharpness，\\n但形式化证明 supremum is attained 被 feasible set 的非凸拓扑阻断。\\n\\nCoverage 略低于 nominal（average 91.3% at 95% nominal）因为 ASV bounds 在已知 exact C 下推导，\\n而 MC 用的是有限样本估计的 C。Gap（3.7%）反映估计不确定性而非 bound failure。\\n\"\n774\t  },\n775\t  {\n776\t    \"name\": \"ASV MC Validation for M-bias, Instrument, Front-door\",\n777\t    \"description\": \"推导剩余 3 个拓扑的 ASV 表达式 + MC 验证。\\nMonotonicity 和 coverage 验证。Sharpness 作为 conjectures + numerical evidence。\\n\",\n778\t    \"results\": {\n779\t      \"monotonicity_holds\": [\n780\t        \"M-bias\",\n781\t        \"instrument\",\n782\t        \"front-door\"\n783\t      ],\n784\t      \"monotonicity_failures\": 0,\n785\t      \"sharpness_numerical\": {\n786\t        \"mbias\": \"achieving 92% of bound\",\n787\t        \"instrument\": \"achieving 89% of bound\",\n788\t        \"frontdoor\": \"achieving 94% of bound\"\n789\t      },\n790\t      \"coverage_at_95_nominal\": {\n791\t        \"mbias\": 0.9,\n792\t        \"instrument\": 0.89,\n793\t        \"frontdoor\": 0.91\n794\t      },\n795\t      \"instrument_conservatism\": \"ASV bounds 1.8× wider than necessary\",\n796\t      \"total_asv_coverage_6_topologies\": 0.907\n797\t    },\n798\t    \"tables\": [\n799\t      {\n800\t        \"name\": \"ASV Results for Secondary Topologies\",\n801\t        \"columns\": [\n802\t          \"topology\",\n803\t          \"monotonicity\",\n804\t          \"sharpness_numerical_pct\",\n805\t          \"coverage_95\",\n806\t          \"conservatism\"\n807\t        ],\n808\t        \"rows\": [\n809\t          [\n810\t            \"M-bias\",\n811\t            \"holds\",\n812\t            \"92%\",\n813\t            0.9,\n814\t            \"comparable to collider\"\n815\t          ],\n816\t          [\n817\t            \"instrument\",\n818\t            \"holds\",\n819\t            \"89%\",\n820\t            0.89,\n821\t            \"1.8× conservative (Wald ratio)\"\n822\t          ],\n823\t          [\n824\t            \"front-door\",\n825\t            \"holds\",\n826\t            \"94%\",\n827\t            0.91,\n828\t            \"near-tight\"\n829\t          ]\n830\t        ]\n831\t      },\n832\t      {\n833\t        \"name\": \"All 6 Topologies ASV Summary\",\n834\t        \"columns\": [\n835\t          \"topology\",\n836\t          \"monotonicity\",\n837\t          \"sharpness_status\",\n838\t          \"coverage_95\"\n839\t        ],\n840\t        \"rows\": [\n841\t          [\n842\t            \"confounding\",\n843\t            \"proved\",\n844\t            \"proved (formal)\",\n845\t            0.93\n846\t          ],\n847\t          [\n848\t            \"mediation\",\n849\t            \"proved\",\n850\t            \"proved (formal)\",\n851\t            0.9\n852\t          ],\n853\t          [\n854\t            \"collider\",\n855\t            \"proved\",\n856\t            \"93% numerical\",\n857\t            0.91\n858\t          ],\n859\t          [\n860\t            \"M-bias\",\n861\t            \"proved\",\n862\t            \"92% numerical\",\n863\t            0.9\n864\t          ],\n865\t          [\n866\t            \"instrument\",\n867\t            \"proved\",\n868\t            \"89% numerical\",\n869\t            0.89\n870\t          ],\n871\t          [\n872\t            \"front-door\",\n873\t            \"proved\",\n874\t            \"94% numerical\",\n875\t            0.91\n876\t          ]\n877\t        ]\n878\t      }\n879\t    ],\n880\t    \"figures\": [],\n881\t    \"analysis\": \"6 个拓扑全部有 ASV 表达式 + validated monotonicity。Sharpness landscape：\\n2 proved (confounding, mediation) + 4 numerical (collider 93%, front-door 94%, M-bias 92%, instrument 89%)。\\nInstrument 是最弱环节——ASV 保守性限制了实用性。论文应诚实讨论并标记 tighter instrument-specific bounds 为 future work。\\nOverall average 95%-nominal coverage = 0.907，在 median 档 [0.88, 0.93] 范围内。\\n\\n\\nMonotonicity 对所有 3 个拓扑成立——与 plan_004 相同的结构性论证：\\nASV 是 minimum-over-perturbation 量，在 perturbation budget δ 中固有单调。\\n\\nSharpness numerical evidence 有差异：front-door 最接近 tight（94%，identification structure 较简单），\\nM-bias 中等（92%），instrument 最远（89%）。\\nInstrument gap 反映 Wald estimator 的 ratio structure——supremum 涉及优化 misclassified 量的 ratio，\\nlandscape 有多个 local optima。\\n\\nInstrument ASV 显著保守（1.8× wider）因为 Wald estimator 放大小分母扰动，\\nworst-case bound 比 typical case 差很多。这是 IV sensitivity analysis 的已知问题（非本框架特有）。\\n\"\n882\t  },\n883\t  {\n884\t    \"name\": \"ASV Calibration on Empirical Data\",\n885\t    \"description\": \"将 ASVs 应用于 plan_003 的经验 confusion matrices，跨 3 CSS tasks × 3 LLMs。\\n在 held-out gold-standard splits 上验证 coverage。\\n比较 ASV 可解释性与 raw confusion matrix reporting。\\n\",\n886\t    \"results\": {\n887\t      \"total_scenarios\": 9,\n888\t      \"empirical_asv_concordance\": 7,\n889\t      \"concordance_failures\": 2,\n890\t      \"failure_scenarios\": [\n891\t        \"toxicity-Llama4 vs toxicity-Qwen35\",\n892\t        \"toxicity-Qwen35 vs toxicity-DeepSeek\"\n893\t      ],\n894\t      \"failure_reason\": \"all 3 models produce high ASVs (>2.0) for toxicity K=2; differences within estimation noise\",\n895\t      \"asv_ranking\": {\n896\t        \"protest\": \"DeepSeek (0.91) > Llama4 (0.82) > Qwen35 (0.68) — correct\",\n897\t        \"stance\": \"DeepSeek (1.41) > Llama4 (1.24) > Qwen35 (1.08) — correct\",\n898\t        \"toxicity\": \"DeepSeek (2.44) ≈ Llama4 (2.31) ≈ Qwen35 (2.18) — indistinguishable\"\n899\t      },\n900\t      \"held_out_coverage_95\": 0.89\n901\t    },\n902\t    \"tables\": [\n903\t      {\n904\t        \"name\": \"ASV Values and Concordance by Task × Model\",\n905\t        \"columns\": [\n906\t          \"task\",\n907\t          \"model\",\n908\t          \"ASV_95\",\n909\t          \"observed_abs_bias\",\n910\t          \"robust_flag\",\n911\t          \"concordant\"\n912\t        ],\n913\t        \"rows\": [\n914\t          [\n915\t            \"protest\",\n916\t            \"Llama 4\",\n917\t            0.82,\n918\t            0.09,\n919\t            \"moderate\",\n920\t            true\n921\t          ],\n922\t          [\n923\t            \"protest\",\n924\t            \"Qwen 3.5\",\n925\t            0.68,\n926\t            0.12,\n927\t            \"fragile\",\n928\t            true\n929\t          ],\n930\t          [\n931\t            \"protest\",\n932\t            \"DeepSeek\",\n933\t            0.91,\n934\t            0.05,\n935\t            \"moderate-high\",\n936\t            true\n937\t          ],\n938\t          [\n939\t            \"stance\",\n940\t            \"Llama 4\",\n941\t            1.24,\n942\t            0.06,\n943\t            \"moderate-high\",\n944\t            true\n945\t          ],\n946\t          [\n947\t            \"stance\",\n948\t            \"Qwen 3.5\",\n949\t            1.08,\n950\t            0.08,\n951\t            \"moderate\",\n952\t            true\n953\t          ],\n954\t          [\n955\t            \"stance\",\n956\t            \"DeepSeek\",\n957\t            1.41,\n958\t            0.03,\n959\t            \"high\",\n960\t            true\n961\t          ],\n962\t          [\n963\t            \"toxicity\",\n964\t            \"Llama 4\",\n965\t            2.31,\n966\t            0.02,\n967\t            \"high\",\n968\t            true\n969\t          ],\n970\t          [\n971\t            \"toxicity\",\n972\t            \"Qwen 3.5\",\n973\t            2.18,\n974\t            0.04,\n975\t            \"high\",\n976\t            false\n977\t          ],\n978\t          [\n979\t            \"toxicity\",\n980\t            \"DeepSeek\",\n981\t            2.44,\n982\t            0.01,\n983\t            \"high\",\n984\t            false\n985\t          ]\n986\t        ]\n987\t      }\n988\t    ],\n989\t    \"figures\": [],\n990\t    \"analysis\": \"ASVs 在 moderate-to-high bias scenarios 中具有经验实用性（protest K=5, stance K=3），\\n但在 low-bias regime 失去区分力（toxicity K=2）。这是诚实且预期的——\\n类似 E-values 在 confounding 小时不 informative。\\n论文应 frame 为：\\\"ASVs are most valuable when annotation error is non-trivial (K≥3, accuracy <0.85)——\\nprecisely the scenarios where researchers lack existing diagnostic tools。\\\"\\n7/9 concordance 支持 Claim 2 的实用价值。\\n\\n\\nConcordance 7/9：ASV 在 protest (K=5) 和 stance (K=3) 任务上正确排序模型鲁棒性——\\n这些任务的 confusion matrix 差异足够大，产生有区分力的 ASV 值。\\nFailure 出现在 toxicity (K=2)：所有 3 个模型有 near-diagonal C（accuracy > 0.86），\\n产生高 ASVs (>2.0)，差异在 MC estimation noise 内——无法区分模型。\\n\\n这是 low-bias regime 的结构性限制：annotation quality 高时（K=2 toxicity），\\nASVs 正确指示\\\"robust\\\"但不能 rank-order models。\\n这实际上是合适的——如果所有模型产生 negligible bias，ranking 本身就无信息量。\\n\\nHeld-out coverage (0.89 at 95% nominal) 略低于 MC coverage (0.91) 因为 empirical C 有额外的\\ngold-standard sample size 估计噪声。Gap 小且在预期范围内。\\n\"\n991\t  },\n992\t  {\n993\t    \"name\": \"Correction Guidance Framework: Decision Mapping and Validation\",\n994\t    \"description\": \"Decision framework: {topology × error structure × ASV} → correction method\\n(DSL / PPI / MLA / naive plug-in / \\\"no existing method adequate\\\")。\\nMC validation: 90 scenarios + empirical validation on plan_003 data。\\n\",\n995\t    \"results\": {\n996\t      \"total_mc_scenarios\": 90,\n997\t      \"correction_framework_accuracy\": 0.89,\n998\t      \"correct_recommendations\": 80,\n999\t      \"boundary_indistinguishable_cases\": 3,\n1000\t      \"hard_failure_cases\": 7,\n1001\t      \"failure_breakdown\": {\n1002\t        \"near_diagonal_all_methods_equivalent\": 3,\n1003\t        \"differential_intermediate_mismatch\": 2,\n1004\t        \"false_recommendation_in_hopeless_regime\": 2\n1005\t      },\n1006\t      \"method_dominance\": {\n1007\t        \"DSL\": \"best in 28/90 (diagonal-dominant C, confounding/mediation)\",\n1008\t        \"PPI\": \"best in 22/90 (moderate C, exposure/front-door)\",\n1009\t        \"MLA\": \"best in 18/90 (high off-diagonal, confounding/collider)\",\n1010\t        \"naive_plugin\": \"best in 12/90 (near-diagonal, any topology)\",\n1011\t        \"no_method_adequate\": \"10/90 (near-permutation + reversal topologies)\"\n1012\t      },\n1013\t      \"empirical_validation_plan003\": {\n1014\t        \"protest_correct\": true,\n1015\t        \"stance_correct\": true,\n1016\t        \"toxicity_correct\": true\n1017\t      },\n1018\t      \"open_problems\": [\n1019\t        \"dependence-aware multi-LLM correction\",\n1020\t        \"differential K≥3 error correction\",\n1021\t        \"collider + near-permutation C (no method reduces bias below 50%)\"\n1022\t      ]\n1023\t    },\n1024\t    \"tables\": [\n1025\t      {\n1026\t        \"name\": \"Correction Method Dominance Map\",\n1027\t        \"columns\": [\n1028\t          \"method\",\n1029\t          \"best_in_n\",\n1030\t          \"primary_topology\",\n1031\t          \"primary_error_regime\"\n1032\t        ],\n1033\t        \"rows\": [\n1034\t          [\n1035\t            \"DSL\",\n1036\t            28,\n1037\t            \"confounding, mediation\",\n1038\t            \"diagonal-dominant C\"\n1039\t          ],\n1040\t          [\n1041\t            \"PPI\",\n1042\t            22,\n1043\t            \"exposure, front-door\",\n1044\t            \"moderate off-diagonal\"\n1045\t          ],\n1046\t          [\n1047\t            \"MLA\",\n1048\t            18,\n1049\t            \"confounding, collider\",\n1050\t            \"high off-diagonal\"\n1051\t          ],\n1052\t          [\n1053\t            \"naive plug-in\",\n1054\t            12,\n1055\t            \"any\",\n1056\t            \"near-diagonal\"\n1057\t          ],\n1058\t          [\n1059\t            \"no method\",\n1060\t            10,\n1061\t            \"exposure, mediation\",\n1062\t            \"near-permutation\"\n1063\t          ]\n1064\t        ]\n1065\t      },\n1066\t      {\n1067\t        \"name\": \"Framework Failure Analysis\",\n1068\t        \"columns\": [\n1069\t          \"failure_type\",\n1070\t          \"count\",\n1071\t          \"impact\",\n1072\t          \"mitigation\"\n1073\t        ],\n1074\t        \"rows\": [\n1075\t          [\n1076\t            \"boundary (methods ≤5% apart)\",\n1077\t            3,\n1078\t            \"low\",\n1079\t            \"any recommendation acceptable\"\n1080\t          ],\n1081\t          [\n1082\t            \"differential mismatch\",\n1083\t            2,\n1084\t            \"moderate\",\n1085\t            \"add continuous differentiality parameter\"\n1086\t          ],\n1087\t          [\n1088\t            \"false recommendation in hopeless regime\",\n1089\t            2,\n1090\t            \"high\",\n1091\t            \"add safety check: if reversal topology + extreme C → flag\"\n1092\t          ]\n1093\t        ]\n1094\t      }\n1095\t    ],\n1096\t    \"figures\": [],\n1097\t    \"analysis\": \"Correction framework 达到主要目标：89% 正确识别 best correction method。\\n11% failure rate 集中在固有歧义的 boundary cases（3%）和真正困难的 regimes（8%）。\\n2 个\\\"false recommendation in hopeless regime\\\"最令人担忧——框架提供了虚假信心。\\n论文应明确讨论此风险并建议 practitioners 始终在 held-out data 上验证 corrections。\\n10 个\\\"no method adequate\\\"scenarios 是论文对 open problems 的贡献——\\n特别是 dependence-aware multi-LLM correction（结合 plan_003 的 correlation 发现）。\\n\\n\\n89% accuracy 反映框架在 clear-cut scenarios（方法性能明显分离）的优势和 boundary cases 的弱点。\\n\\n3 个 boundary cases 是结构性不可区分的：near-diagonal C（low error）下所有方法结果相近（within 5%），\\n\\\"best\\\" recommendation 是任意的。这不是框架的失败而是问题本身的 degeneracy。\\n\\n7 个 hard failures：\\n(a) 3 cases: near-diagonal C 使所有方法等效但框架因 threshold effects 选了次优方法；\\n(b) 2 cases: intermediate differential error 处框架的 non-differential/differential 二分类\\n无法捕获 differentiality 的连续性质；\\n(c) 2 cases: 框架推荐了方法但正确答案是\\\"no method adequate\\\"（near-permutation C + reversal topology）。\\n\\nMethod dominance 是 topology-driven 的：DSL 擅长 confounding（调整 misclassified confounder 是其 native use case），\\nPPI 擅长 exposure（regression-calibration 处理 treatment misclassification），\\nMLA 擅长 high off-diagonal error（maximum likelihood 直接建模 C）。\\n\\n10/90 \\\"no method adequate\\\" 集中在 reversal topologies（exposure, mediation）+ extreme C——\\n这些是 current correction literature 的真实 gaps。\\n\"\n1098\t  },\n1099\t  {\n1100\t    \"name\": \"Pathological Confusion Matrix Analysis\",\n1101\t    \"description\": \"极端 C 结构分析：near-permutation, rank-deficient, block-diagonal。\\n刻画 catastrophic bias 条件并识别结构性预测因子。\\n\",\n1102\t    \"results\": {\n1103\t      \"spectral_gap_predictive_R2\": 0.78,\n1104\t      \"diagonal_dominance_predictive_R2\": 0.71,\n1105\t      \"combined_predictor_R2\": 0.84,\n1106\t      \"catastrophic_threshold_spectral_gap\": 0.3,\n1107\t      \"catastrophic_threshold_diagonal_dominance\": 0.5,\n1108\t      \"near_permutation_universally_catastrophic\": true,\n1109\t      \"rank_deficient_topology_dependent\": true,\n1110\t      \"rank_deficient_worst\": [\n1111\t        \"front-door\",\n1112\t        \"instrument\"\n1113\t      ],\n1114\t      \"block_diagonal_worst\": \"mediation (blocks indirect path)\"\n1115\t    },\n1116\t    \"tables\": [\n1117\t      {\n1118\t        \"name\": \"Structural Predictors of Bias Severity\",\n1119\t        \"columns\": [\n1120\t          \"predictor\",\n1121\t          \"R2_overall\",\n1122\t          \"best_topology_R2\",\n1123\t          \"worst_topology_R2\"\n1124\t        ],\n1125\t        \"rows\": [\n1126\t          [\n1127\t            \"spectral gap\",\n1128\t            0.78,\n1129\t            \"exposure (0.85)\",\n1130\t            \"M-bias (0.67)\"\n1131\t          ],\n1132\t          [\n1133\t            \"diagonal dominance\",\n1134\t            0.71,\n1135\t            \"confounding (0.82)\",\n1136\t            \"front-door (0.58)\"\n1137\t          ],\n1138\t          [\n1139\t            \"spectral gap + diag dom\",\n1140\t            0.84,\n1141\t            \"exposure (0.91)\",\n1142\t            \"instrument (0.74)\"\n1143\t          ]\n1144\t        ]\n1145\t      },\n1146\t      {\n1147\t        \"name\": \"Catastrophic Bias Conditions by Topology and C Structure\",\n1148\t        \"columns\": [\n1149\t          \"topology\",\n1150\t          \"near_permutation\",\n1151\t          \"rank_deficient\",\n1152\t          \"block_diagonal\"\n1153\t        ],\n1154\t        \"rows\": [\n1155\t          [\n1156\t            \"confounding\",\n1157\t            \"severe (OVB > 2×)\",\n1158\t            \"moderate\",\n1159\t            \"moderate\"\n1160\t          ],\n1161\t          [\n1162\t            \"exposure\",\n1163\t            \"catastrophic (reversal)\",\n1164\t            \"severe\",\n1165\t            \"severe (block reversal)\"\n1166\t          ],\n1167\t          [\n1168\t            \"mediation\",\n1169\t            \"severe (reversal)\",\n1170\t            \"moderate\",\n1171\t            \"severe (block indirect effects)\"\n1172\t          ],\n1173\t          [\n1174\t            \"collider\",\n1175\t            \"severe (attenuation > 60%)\",\n1176\t            \"moderate\",\n1177\t            \"moderate\"\n1178\t          ],\n1179\t          [\n1180\t            \"M-bias\",\n1181\t            \"moderate\",\n1182\t            \"moderate\",\n1183\t            \"mild\"\n1184\t          ],\n1185\t          [\n1186\t            \"instrument\",\n1187\t            \"moderate\",\n1188\t            \"catastrophic (Wald denom → 0)\",\n1189\t            \"moderate\"\n1190\t          ],\n1191\t          [\n1192\t            \"front-door\",\n1193\t            \"moderate\",\n1194\t            \"catastrophic (identification loss)\",\n1195\t            \"moderate\"\n1196\t          ]\n1197\t        ]\n1198\t      }\n1199\t    ],\n1200\t    \"figures\": [],\n1201\t    \"analysis\": \"实用 takeaway：spectral gap < 0.3 OR diagonal dominance < 0.5 → 所有拓扑均高风险。\\n这一双阈值规则足够简单可用且捕获 84% 的 bias variance。\\nFront-door 和 instrument 对 rank-deficient C 特别脆弱（ratio estimator 分母问题）。\\n这些 structural predictors 是 toolkit (plan_010) 的 automatic diagnostic features 候选。\\n\\n\\nSpectral gap（C 的第一和第二 eigenvalue 之差）预测 bias severity（R²=0.78）\\n因为它捕获了 C 距 permutation matrix 的距离——反转的结构性来源。\\nR²=0.78 表示强但不完美的预测；剩余方差来自 topology-specific interactions。\\n\\nDiagonal dominance（minimum diagonal element）是更简单的 proxy，R² 略低（0.71）。\\nCombined spectral gap + diagonal dominance 达到 R²=0.84——两个 features 捕获了大部分 bias-relevant C structure。\\n\\nNear-permutation 普遍 catastrophic 因为 label-swapping 搅乱所有拓扑。\\nRank-deficient C 是 topology-dependent：front-door 和 instrument 的 identification formula\\n含有 C-dependent 分母——C rank-deficient 时分母趋零，bias unbounded。\\nConfounding/mediation/collider 对 rank deficiency 处理更 graceful（无 ratio estimator）。\\n\\nBlock-diagonal C 对 mediation 最 severe——block 结构可以创造 artifact category boundaries 上的 apparent indirect effects。\\n\"\n1202\t  },\n1203\t  {\n1204\t    \"name\": \"annot-sensitivity Python Toolkit\",\n1205\t    \"description\": \"Open-source pip-installable package：user-specified DAG + confusion matrix + downstream estimate\\n→ bias expressions + ASV + sensitivity curves + correction recommendation + diagnostic plots。\\n\",\n1206\t    \"results\": {\n1207\t      \"package_name\": \"annot-sensitivity\",\n1208\t      \"supported_topologies\": 6,\n1209\t      \"supported_K_range\": \"2–10\",\n1210\t      \"core_api\": [\n1211\t        \"compute_bias(dag, C, estimate) → BiasResult\",\n1212\t        \"compute_asv(dag, C, estimate, delta_range) → ASVResult\",\n1213\t        \"recommend_correction(dag, C, asv) → CorrectionRecommendation\",\n1214\t        \"diagnostic_plot(result) → Figure\",\n1215\t        \"eigendecomp_summary(C, K) → EigenSummary\",\n1216\t        \"check_pathological(C) → PathologyReport (spectral gap + diag dom thresholds)\"\n1217\t      ],\n1218\t      \"worked_examples\": 3,\n1219\t      \"example_topologies\": [\n1220\t        \"confounding (baseline)\",\n1221\t        \"exposure (reversal)\",\n1222\t        \"mediation (conditional reversal)\"\n1223\t      ],\n1224\t      \"test_coverage\": 0.87,\n1225\t      \"documentation\": \"API reference + 3 tutorial notebooks + quick-start guide\",\n1226\t      \"known_limitations\": [\n1227\t        \"K>7 eigendecomposition slow (>10s/computation)\",\n1228\t        \"correction accuracy inherits plan_007 limitations (89%)\",\n1229\t        \"CLI + notebook only, no GUI\",\n1230\t        \"3/6 topologies lack detailed tutorials (M-bias, instrument, front-door)\"\n1231\t      ]\n1232\t    },\n1233\t    \"tables\": [],\n1234\t    \"figures\": [],\n1235\t    \"analysis\": \"Toolkit 是 functional deliverable，使论文的理论贡献对 practitioners 可及。\\n3 个 worked examples 覆盖最重要的场景（reversal cases）。\\n主要 gap：3 个拓扑缺少 tutorial，可能限制 M-bias/instrument/front-door 用户的采纳。\\nPost-publication 低成本 follow-up。\\n\\n3 个 worked examples（而非 6）因为 median 档 scope 有限——优先覆盖 3 个 reversal-relevant 拓扑\\n（confounding 作为 baseline，exposure + mediation 作为反转案例）。剩余 3 个拓扑在 API 中支持但缺少详细 tutorial。\\n\\nK>7 性能限制反映 eigendecomposition 的 O(K³) 成本——对典型 CSS 使用（K=3–7）可接受，\\n对罕见 high-K 应用偏慢。\\n\\nTest coverage 0.87 反映核心计算（bias expressions, ASV）的 thorough unit testing\\n和 visualization/correction recommendation 组件的 lighter testing。\\n\\ncheck_pathological() 集成 plan_009 的 spectral gap + diagonal dominance 阈值，\\n为 practitioner 提供自动 C matrix 质量诊断。\\n\"\n1236\t  }\n1237\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25bf0861-1839-4453-8613-912d152b4cb0","uuid":"530dd707-2b01-4a98-a84c-a37268c49fe6","timestamp":"2026-05-20T08:29:41.747Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-prod_0510/projects/causal_annot_error_attrib/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T074549/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"K=3 Bias Expressions and MC Validation Across 6 DAG Topologies\",\n    \"description\": \"对 6 个 DAG 拓扑（confounding, mediation, collider, M-bias, instrument, front-door）推导 K=3 closed-form bias 表达式，\\nMC 验证：1000 reps × N=10000 × 6 confusion matrix structures/topology = 36 scenarios。\\n每个拓扑做 100k random C search 检测方向反转。Confounding 为 MVP 再验证；其余 5 个为新推导。\\n结合 MVP exposure 结果，total reversal topologies = 2。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_scenarios\": 36,\n      \"theory_mc_match\": \"33/36\",\n      \"theory_mc_match_rate\": 0.917,\n      \"reversal_in_plan_001\": 1,\n      \"reversal_topology_new\": \"mediation\",\n      \"combined_reversal_topologies\": 2,\n      \"combined_reversal_list\": [\n        \"exposure (MVP)\",\n        \"mediation (new)\"\n      ],\n      \"confounding\": {\n        \"violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"bias_range\": [\n          0.132,\n          0.298\n        ],\n        \"theory_mc\": \"6/6\",\n        \"mechanism\": \"residual confounding, monotonic toward OVB\"\n      },\n      \"mediation\": {\n        \"violation_rate\": 0.23,\n        \"sign_reversal_rate\": 0.18,\n        \"amplification_rate\": 0.05,\n        \"worst_severity\": 1.62,\n        \"named_structures_with_violation\": \"2/6 (near-permutation, block-off-diagonal)\",\n        \"theory_mc\": \"6/6\",\n        \"reversal_condition\": \"off-diagonal dominance > 0.6 AND |indirect effect| > 0.2\",\n        \"indirect_bias_range\": [\n          -0.18,\n          0.14\n        ]\n      },\n      \"collider\": {\n        \"violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"bias_range\": [\n          0.04,\n          0.21\n        ],\n        \"attenuation_range\": \"15-60% reduction vs no misclassification\",\n        \"theory_mc\": \"5/6\",\n        \"mechanism\": \"misclassification smooths conditioning variable, reduces collider bias magnitude, preserves direction\"\n      },\n      \"mbias\": {\n        \"violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"bias_range\": [\n          0.02,\n          0.16\n        ],\n        \"theory_mc\": \"5/6\",\n        \"mechanism\": \"spurious pathway weakened by misclassification of M-bias variable\"\n      },\n      \"instrument\": {\n        \"violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"bias_range\": [\n          0.03,\n          0.19\n        ],\n        \"theory_mc\": \"6/6\",\n        \"mechanism\": \"instrument weakened, Wald estimator biased toward OLS, direction preserved\"\n      },\n      \"frontdoor\": {\n        \"violation_rate\": 0.0,\n        \"bias_range\": [\n          0.05,\n          0.22\n        ],\n        \"theory_mc\": \"5/6\",\n        \"mechanism\": \"front-door estimate attenuated, identification weakened but direction stable\"\n      },\n      \"mc_mismatch_detail\": \"3 mismatches in collider(1), M-bias(1), front-door(1) — all near-permutation C where MC variance is highest due to complex bias formulas (conditioning, ratio estimators)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Direction Reversal Summary by Topology (plan_001 + MVP exposure)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"topology\",\n          \"misclassified_var\",\n          \"violation_rate\",\n          \"sign_reversal\",\n          \"worst_severity\",\n          \"theory_mc\",\n          \"direction\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"exposure (MVP)\",\n            \"treatment X\",\n            0.85,\n            0.834,\n            2.83,\n            \"5/5\",\n            \"reversal-dominant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"confounding\",\n            \"confounder U\",\n            0.0,\n            0.0,\n            \"1.00×OVB\",\n            \"6/6\",\n            \"monotonic toward OVB\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mediation\",\n            \"mediator M\",\n            0.23,\n            0.18,\n            1.62,\n            \"6/6\",\n            \"conditional reversal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"collider\",\n            \"collider Z\",\n            0.0,\n            0.0,\n            \"0.85×(attenuated)\",\n            \"5/6\",\n            \"monotonic attenuation\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"M-bias\",\n            \"M-bias var\",\n            0.0,\n            0.0,\n            \"0.92×(attenuated)\",\n            \"5/6\",\n            \"monotonic attenuation\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"instrument\",\n            \"instrument Z\",\n            0.0,\n            0.0,\n            \"0.78×(toward OLS)\",\n            \"6/6\",\n            \"monotonic toward OLS\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"front-door\",\n            \"front-door M\",\n            0.0,\n            0.0,\n            \"0.88×(attenuated)\",\n            \"5/6\",\n            \"monotonic attenuation\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Mediation Reversal Conditions (100k Random C, K=3)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"C_structure_category\",\n          \"pct_of_random_C\",\n          \"violation_rate\",\n          \"sign_reversal_rate\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"near-permutation (off-diag dom > 0.6)\",\n            \"30%\",\n            0.57,\n            0.44\n          ],\n          [\n            \"moderate (off-diag dom 0.3–0.6)\",\n            \"40%\",\n            0.14,\n            0.09\n          ],\n          [\n            \"diagonal-dominant (off-diag dom < 0.3)\",\n            \"30%\",\n            0.0,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"overall\",\n            \"100%\",\n            0.23,\n            0.18\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"plan_001 确认 median 档的核心结果：6 个拓扑中仅 mediation 出现新的反转（结合 MVP exposure = 2 个反转拓扑）。\\n关键发现是反转机制的不对称性：exposure 是\\\"广泛性反转\\\"（label swap 直接作用于 treatment 对比），\\nmediation 是\\\"条件性反转\\\"（需双重门控：C 足够非对角 + 间接效应足够大）。\\n这一不对称性本身就是论文的核心贡献——它证明了 direction reversal 是 topology-specific 的，\\n不能仅从 confusion matrix 结构预测，必须结合 DAG 拓扑分析。\\n4 个单调拓扑的 magnitude 变异（如 collider 0.04–0.21）支持补充论据：即使方向保持，\\nbias magnitude 仍不可从 binary 框架预测。\\n需要补充实验：对 mediation 的 phase diagram 做更精细的 grid search（Fig 3 的分辨率不够用于实用指导）。\\n\\n\\nMediation（23% violation）：misclassifying mediator M 影响间接路径 X→M→Y。反转需要双重门控：\\n(a) C matrix off-diagonal dominance > 0.6（标签大幅置换），AND (b) |true indirect effect| > 0.2（间接效应足够大可以被反转）。\\n因为间接效应 = X→M 系数 × M→Y 系数的乘积，两条路径都必须被实质性扰动才能反转——这种双重门控将 violation rate 限制在 23%。\\n对比 exposure（MVP 85% violation）：exposure misclassification 直接作用于单一 X→Y 路径，无衰减机制，几乎所有非对角 C 都触发反转。\\n这一机制差异（直接路径 vs 乘积路径）是 median 档的核心发现——direction reversal 是 topology-specific 的。\\n\\nCollider（0% violation）：misclassifying Z（collider）并 conditioning on Z* 时，误分类平滑了 Z 的分布，\\n削弱了 selection effect 的强度但不改变其方向。方向由结构方程的符号决定（与测量质量无关）。\\n100k random C 中无一例外。\\n\\nM-bias/Instrument/Front-door（0% violation）：这些拓扑涉及辅助变量，misclassification 削弱 identification 但不反转估计方向。\\nInstrument 特殊之处在于 Wald estimator 的分母受影响（偏向 OLS），但符号不变。\\nFront-door 的 double summation 使 MC 方差在极端 C 下偏高，导致 1/6 mismatch。\\n\\n3 个 MC mismatch 均出现在 near-permutation C structure 下——这些拓扑的 bias formula 含有 conditioning 或 ratio 结构，\\nMC 在极端 C 下方差更大，理论值落在 95% CI 边缘外。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"General-K Matrix Bias Expressions and Interpretability Tools\",\n    \"description\": \"将 bias 表达式扩展到 K=5,7 的矩阵形式。开发 3 个可解释性工具：\\n(a) eigendecomposition summaries，(b) worst-case scalar bounds，(c) diagnostic visualizations。\\n在 confounding + mediation + collider + exposure DAGs 上验证 K=5,7。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"K5_theory_mc_match_rate\": 0.89,\n      \"K7_theory_mc_match_rate\": 0.85,\n      \"K5_scenarios_tested\": 24,\n      \"K7_scenarios_tested\": 24,\n      \"eigendecomp_variance_explained_top2_K5\": {\n        \"confounding\": 0.87,\n        \"exposure\": 0.91,\n        \"mediation\": 0.83,\n        \"collider\": 0.88\n      },\n      \"eigendecomp_variance_explained_top3_K7\": {\n        \"confounding\": 0.84,\n        \"exposure\": 0.88,\n        \"mediation\": 0.8,\n        \"collider\": 0.85\n      },\n      \"worst_case_bound_conservatism_median\": \"2.6×\",\n      \"worst_case_bound_conservatism_range\": \"2.1–3.4×\",\n      \"K5_exposure_violation_rate\": 0.88,\n      \"K5_mediation_violation_rate\": 0.28,\n      \"K7_exposure_violation_rate\": 0.9,\n      \"K7_mediation_violation_rate\": 0.31,\n      \"reversal_pattern_persistence\": true,\n      \"dominant_eigenmode_interpretation\": {\n        \"mode_1\": \"diagonal dominance deviation (how far C is from identity)\",\n        \"mode_2\": \"permutation component (which off-diagonal entries dominate)\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Eigendecomposition: Variance Explained by Top Modes\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"topology\",\n          \"K\",\n          \"mode_1\",\n          \"mode_2\",\n          \"mode_3\",\n          \"cumulative_top2\",\n          \"cumulative_top3\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"confounding\",\n            5,\n            0.68,\n            0.19,\n            0.08,\n            0.87,\n            0.95\n          ],\n          [\n            \"confounding\",\n            7,\n            0.59,\n            0.17,\n            0.08,\n            0.76,\n            0.84\n          ],\n          [\n            \"exposure\",\n            5,\n            0.74,\n            0.17,\n            0.05,\n            0.91,\n            0.96\n          ],\n          [\n            \"exposure\",\n            7,\n            0.65,\n            0.15,\n            0.08,\n            0.8,\n            0.88\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mediation\",\n            5,\n            0.61,\n            0.22,\n            0.09,\n            0.83,\n            0.92\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mediation\",\n            7,\n            0.52,\n            0.19,\n            0.09,\n            0.71,\n            0.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"collider\",\n            5,\n            0.7,\n            0.18,\n            0.06,\n            0.88,\n            0.94\n          ],\n          [\n            \"collider\",\n            7,\n            0.62,\n            0.16,\n            0.07,\n            0.78,\n            0.85\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Violation Rate Scaling with K\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"topology\",\n          \"K=3\",\n          \"K=5\",\n          \"K=7\",\n          \"trend\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"exposure\",\n            0.85,\n            0.88,\n            0.9,\n            \"near saturation\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mediation\",\n            0.23,\n            0.28,\n            0.31,\n            \"monotonic increase\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"confounding\",\n            0.0,\n            0.0,\n            0.0,\n            \"flat (monotonic)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"collider\",\n            0.0,\n            0.0,\n            0.0,\n            \"flat (monotonic)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Matrix-form 表达式成功泛化 K=3 结果。实用发现：top 2 eigenmodes 在 K≤5 下足够（>83% 方差解释），\\nK=7 可能需要 3 个 modes。这指导 toolkit 设计——默认 2-mode summary 加可选扩展。\\nReversal patterns 在 K=5,7 持续，确认 K=3 理论分析不是 special case。\\nWorst-case bounds 的保守性（2.6×）是 tradeoff：tight bounds 需要 topology-specific 优化（随 K 扩展性差），\\nconservative bounds 计算快且作为安全边界仍有实用价值。\\n\\n\\nK=5,7 的 match rate 低于 K=3（0.89/0.85 vs 0.917）因为 MC 方差随 C 的自由参数数 K(K-1) 增长——K=5 有 20 个自由参数，K=7 有 42 个，\\n相同 MC replications 下 confidence interval 更宽。\\n\\nEigendecomposition 的 top 2 modes 能解释 83–91% 方差，因为实际 confusion matrix 具有低有效秩结构：\\n主导误差模式是\\\"相邻类别混淆\\\"（语义相似的类别被混淆），产生带对角扰动结构，被 2–3 个 eigenmodes 良好捕获。\\nMediation 的方差解释率略低（0.83 K=5）因为间接效应涉及乘积，放大了二阶 eigenmode 的贡献。\\n\\nWorst-case bounds 保守（median 2.6×）因为它们对给定 diagonal dominance 下所有 C 做极值优化，\\n包括实际罕见的对抗性配置。作为安全边界是可接受的——类似 E-values 的保守性。\\n\\nViolation rates 随 K 轻微上升（mediation 23% → 28% → 31%）因为更大的 K 增加了 off-diagonal confusion 路径，\\n使 label permutation 更可能。Exposure 接近饱和（85% → 88% → 90%）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Empirical Confusion Matrices: 3 LLMs × 3 CSS Tasks\",\n    \"description\": \"从 Llama 4 Maverick, Qwen 3.5 Plus, DeepSeek V4 收集经验 confusion matrices。\\n3 个 CSS 任务：protest event coding (K=5, ACLED), stance detection (K=3, SemEval/VAST), toxicity (K=2, Civil Comments)。\\n~30K annotations/model × 3 tasks × 3 prompt variants = ~270K total annotations。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"api_cost_actual\": \"$420\",\n      \"total_annotations\": 270000,\n      \"protest_K5\": {\n        \"llama4_macro_f1\": 0.71,\n        \"llama4_accuracy\": 0.74,\n        \"qwen35_macro_f1\": 0.68,\n        \"qwen35_accuracy\": 0.71,\n        \"deepseek_macro_f1\": 0.73,\n        \"deepseek_accuracy\": 0.76,\n        \"inter_model_error_agreement\": 0.58,\n        \"downstream_bias_range_abs\": [\n          0.05,\n          0.12\n        ],\n        \"dominant_error_pattern\": \"adjacent-category confusion (riot↔protest, strategic↔organized)\"\n      },\n      \"stance_K3\": {\n        \"llama4_macro_f1\": 0.76,\n        \"llama4_accuracy\": 0.79,\n        \"qwen35_macro_f1\": 0.74,\n        \"qwen35_accuracy\": 0.77,\n        \"deepseek_macro_f1\": 0.78,\n        \"deepseek_accuracy\": 0.81,\n        \"inter_model_error_agreement\": 0.62,\n        \"downstream_bias_range_abs\": [\n          0.03,\n          0.08\n        ],\n        \"dominant_error_pattern\": \"neutral-as-default bias (favor→neutral, against→neutral)\"\n      },\n      \"toxicity_K2\": {\n        \"llama4_f1\": 0.88,\n        \"llama4_accuracy\": 0.9,\n        \"qwen35_f1\": 0.86,\n        \"qwen35_accuracy\": 0.88,\n        \"deepseek_f1\": 0.89,\n        \"deepseek_accuracy\": 0.91,\n        \"inter_model_error_agreement\": 0.64,\n        \"downstream_bias_range_abs\": [\n          0.01,\n          0.04\n        ],\n        \"dominant_error_pattern\": \"slight FN bias (under-flagging toxicity)\"\n      },\n      \"prompt_variant_stability\": \"macro-F1 varies ±0.03; confusion matrix structure stable across prompts\",\n      \"cross_model_error_correlation_mean\": 0.61\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Empirical Performance Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"task\",\n          \"K\",\n          \"model\",\n          \"macro_F1\",\n          \"accuracy\",\n          \"dominant_error\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"protest\",\n            5,\n            \"Llama 4 Maverick\",\n            0.71,\n            0.74,\n            \"riot↔protest (0.15)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"protest\",\n            5,\n            \"Qwen 3.5 Plus\",\n            0.68,\n            0.71,\n            \"riot↔protest (0.18), remote↔organized (0.12)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"protest\",\n            5,\n            \"DeepSeek V4\",\n            0.73,\n            0.76,\n            \"riot↔protest (0.13)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"stance\",\n            3,\n            \"Llama 4 Maverick\",\n            0.76,\n            0.79,\n            \"favor→neutral (0.18)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"stance\",\n            3,\n            \"Qwen 3.5 Plus\",\n            0.74,\n            0.77,\n            \"favor→neutral (0.21), against→neutral (0.14)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"stance\",\n            3,\n            \"DeepSeek V4\",\n            0.78,\n            0.81,\n            \"favor→neutral (0.15)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"toxicity\",\n            2,\n            \"Llama 4 Maverick\",\n            0.88,\n            0.9,\n            \"FN toxic→non-toxic (0.12)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"toxicity\",\n            2,\n            \"Qwen 3.5 Plus\",\n            0.86,\n            0.88,\n            \"FN toxic→non-toxic (0.14)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"toxicity\",\n            2,\n            \"DeepSeek V4\",\n            0.89,\n            0.91,\n            \"FN toxic→non-toxic (0.10)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Inter-Model Error Correlation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"task\",\n          \"model_pair\",\n          \"error_agreement_when_both_err\",\n          \"kappa_on_errors\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"protest\",\n            \"Llama4–Qwen35\",\n            0.56,\n            0.31\n          ],\n          [\n            \"protest\",\n            \"Llama4–DeepSeek\",\n            0.61,\n            0.38\n          ],\n          [\n            \"protest\",\n            \"Qwen35–DeepSeek\",\n            0.57,\n            0.33\n          ],\n          [\n            \"stance\",\n            \"Llama4–Qwen35\",\n            0.6,\n            0.35\n          ],\n          [\n            \"stance\",\n            \"Llama4–DeepSeek\",\n            0.64,\n            0.41\n          ],\n          [\n            \"stance\",\n            \"Qwen35–DeepSeek\",\n            0.62,\n            0.37\n          ],\n          [\n            \"toxicity\",\n            \"Llama4–Qwen35\",\n            0.63,\n            0.39\n          ],\n          [\n            \"toxicity\",\n            \"Llama4–DeepSeek\",\n            0.66,\n            0.44\n          ],\n          [\n            \"toxicity\",\n            \"Qwen35–DeepSeek\",\n            0.64,\n            0.41\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"经验 confusion matrices 确认真实 LLMs 产生 moderately diagonal-dominant 的 C matrix——\\n远离 near-permutation 极端但有足够 off-diagonal mass 产生可检测的 downstream bias。\\n关键经验发现：C structure 是 task-dependent（adjacent-category for protest，neutral-absorbing for stance）\\n且 model-stable（同一 task 下 3 个模型展示相似结构模式）。\\n这意味着理论 taxonomy 的 per-topology 预测适用于真实 LLM 场景——C structure 可从 task 预测，不取决于模型选择。\\nInter-model error correlation 直接支持论文 framing：ensembles 无法修复系统性误差。\\n\\n\\n性能水平反映 2025–2026 LLMs 在 CSS 任务上的典型表现：K=5 protest coding 最难（事件类型间区分微妙），\\nK=3 stance 中等（neutral 类别歧义性高），K=2 toxicity 最易（信号明确）。\\n\\nInter-model error agreement（0.58–0.64）与 Kim et al.（ICML 2025）报告的 ~60% 一致。\\nToxicity 略高因为 binary task 出错方式更少。\\n这验证了论文的动机前提：LLM errors are correlated，ensemble averaging 效果有限。\\n\\nDownstream bias 范围是中等的（非 dramatic）因为真实 LLM confusion matrices 是 moderately diagonal-dominant 的——\\n不是 near-permutation 极端。这是 median 档的预期：理论极端（near-permutation C 导致 2.83× severity）\\n在当前 LLMs 中不会实际出现，但 bias 是可检测的且非 trivial 的。\\n\\nPrompt variant 稳定性（±0.03 F1，C structure stable）支持论文聚焦于 confusion matrix structure 而非 prompt engineering——\\nerror 的结构模式对 prompting 鲁棒，即使边际性能有移动。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Binarization Collapse Analysis Across 6 Topologies\",\n    \"description\": \"对 6 个拓扑在 K=3,5,7 下：将 K-class 变量折叠为 binary，\\n比较 full multi-class bias expression vs binarized expression。\\n评估何时 binarization 安全、何时危险。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"max_delta_overall\": 0.13,\n      \"max_delta_by_K\": {\n        \"K3\": 0.103,\n        \"K5\": 0.13,\n        \"K7\": 0.13\n      },\n      \"worst_delta_topology\": \"mediation (K=5)\",\n      \"binarization_direction_reversal_topologies\": [\n        \"exposure\",\n        \"mediation\"\n      ],\n      \"safe_binarization_topologies\": [\n        \"collider\",\n        \"M-bias\",\n        \"instrument\"\n      ],\n      \"lossy_but_direction_safe\": [\n        \"confounding\",\n        \"front-door\"\n      ],\n      \"delta_by_topology_K3\": {\n        \"confounding\": 0.103,\n        \"mediation\": 0.09,\n        \"collider\": 0.07,\n        \"mbias\": 0.06,\n        \"instrument\": 0.05,\n        \"frontdoor\": 0.08\n      },\n      \"delta_by_topology_K5\": {\n        \"confounding\": 0.11,\n        \"mediation\": 0.13,\n        \"collider\": 0.09,\n        \"mbias\": 0.08,\n        \"instrument\": 0.06,\n        \"frontdoor\": 0.09\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Binarization Delta Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"topology\",\n          \"K\",\n          \"max_delta\",\n          \"direction_reversal_from_binarization\",\n          \"safety_class\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"confounding\",\n            3,\n            0.103,\n            false,\n            \"direction-safe, magnitude-unsafe\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"confounding\",\n            5,\n            0.11,\n            false,\n            \"direction-safe, magnitude-unsafe\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mediation\",\n            3,\n            0.09,\n            true,\n            \"unsafe\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mediation\",\n            5,\n            0.13,\n            true,\n            \"unsafe\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"exposure (ref)\",\n            3,\n            0.09,\n            true,\n            \"unsafe\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"exposure (ref)\",\n            5,\n            0.1,\n            true,\n            \"unsafe\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"collider\",\n            3,\n            0.07,\n            false,\n            \"safe\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"collider\",\n            5,\n            0.09,\n            false,\n            \"safe\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"M-bias\",\n            3,\n            0.06,\n            false,\n            \"safe\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"instrument\",\n            3,\n            0.05,\n            false,\n            \"safe\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"front-door\",\n            3,\n            0.08,\n            false,\n            \"direction-safe, magnitude-marginal\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Binarization 不是逃离 K≥3 复杂性的安全手段。Max delta 0.13（mediation K=5）在典型 CSS 回归中\\n（effect size 0.1–0.5）足以主导估计。\\n拓扑分三组：(1) binarization-unsafe（exposure, mediation——可能反转方向），\\n(2) binarization-lossy（confounding, front-door——保持方向但损失量级精度），\\n(3) binarization-tolerable（collider, M-bias, instrument——delta 小，安全）。\\n这支持论文的 multi-class treatment is necessary 论点。\\n\\n\\nBinarization delta 在 K=5 达到峰值（0.13）并在 K=7 持平，因为 K→2 的信息损失在 K=5–7 饱和——\\n超过 K=7 后额外类别的边际信息递减。\\n\\nMediation 的 delta 最大（K=5 时 0.13）因为 binarizing mediator M 将间接路径折叠为单一对比，\\n丢失了 multi-class expression 捕获的 category-specific indirect effects。\\n对 exposure 和 mediation，某些 binarization folding 产生方向反转：\\n将 category 1+2 vs 3 折叠可能将相反方向的效应分配到同一 binary class。\\n\\nConfounding delta 高（K=3 0.103，来自 MVP）因为 binarizing confounder 丢失了残差混杂控制。\\n但方向保持（direction-safe, magnitude-unsafe）。\\n\\nCollider/M-bias/instrument delta 较小因为这些拓扑涉及辅助变量，\\nbinary 近似更接近 multi-class truth——关键量（induced bias direction）更依赖 conditioning operation 而非变量粒度。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ASV Framework: Formal Proofs for Confounding, Mediation, Collider\",\n    \"description\": \"推导 3 个优先拓扑的 ASV 表达式。形式化证明 monotonicity 和 sharpness。\\nMC 验证：coverage at 90%, 95%, 99% across 1000 scenarios/topology。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"monotonicity_proved\": [\n        \"confounding\",\n        \"mediation\",\n        \"collider\"\n      ],\n      \"sharpness_proved\": [\n        \"confounding\",\n        \"mediation\"\n      ],\n      \"sharpness_incomplete\": [\n        \"collider\"\n      ],\n      \"sharpness_formal_proofs_count\": 2,\n      \"collider_sharpness_numerical\": \"achieving 93% of bound in 10k optimization runs\",\n      \"coverage_at_95_nominal\": {\n        \"confounding\": 0.93,\n        \"mediation\": 0.9,\n        \"collider\": 0.91\n      },\n      \"coverage_at_90_nominal\": {\n        \"confounding\": 0.95,\n        \"mediation\": 0.92,\n        \"collider\": 0.93\n      },\n      \"coverage_at_99_nominal\": {\n        \"confounding\": 0.97,\n        \"mediation\": 0.96,\n        \"collider\": 0.95\n      },\n      \"average_coverage_95\": 0.913\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"ASV Proof Status and Coverage (Priority Topologies)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"topology\",\n          \"monotonicity\",\n          \"sharpness\",\n          \"coverage_90\",\n          \"coverage_95\",\n          \"coverage_99\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"confounding\",\n            \"formal proof\",\n            \"formal proof\",\n            0.95,\n            0.93,\n            0.97\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mediation\",\n            \"formal proof\",\n            \"formal proof\",\n            0.92,\n            0.9,\n            0.96\n          ],\n          [\n            \"collider\",\n            \"formal proof\",\n            \"numerical only (93%)\",\n            0.93,\n            0.91,\n            0.95\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ASV 框架在 3 个优先拓扑上验证：monotonicity universally proved，sharpness 2/3 proved。\\nCollider sharpness gap（7%）是主要技术障碍——论文应增加一段讨论 conditioning-on-misclassified-variable 导致的非凸优化问题，\\n并标记 convex relaxation approach 为 future work。\\nMediation 的更陡 ASV 曲线意味着 mediation DAGs 的结论对 annotation error 更敏感——\\n与 direction reversal 发现一致，自然连接 Claim 1 和 Claim 2。\\n\\n\\nMonotonicity 对所有 3 个拓扑成立（proved）因为：更大的 δ 意味着 sensitivity set 中考虑更极端的 C →\\noverturn conclusion 所需的 minimum perturbation 只能增加或不变。\\n这与 underlying bias 是否单调无关——ASV 是 min-over-C 量，不是 pointwise bias。\\n\\nConfounding sharpness：bias 在 C 的 off-diagonal elements 上是线性的，supremum 有 clean convex structure，\\nsharpness-achieving C 在 feasible set 的顶点。构造性证明。\\n\\nMediation sharpness：尽管存在方向反转，ASV sharpness 仍可证——通过分别分析 attenuation regime 和 reversal regime。\\nReversal boundary 处的 worst-case C 恰好达到 bound——构造性证明利用 phase transition 结构。\\n这是一个 nice 的结果：有反转的拓扑仍然有 tight bound，加强了 ASV 框架的可信度。\\n\\nCollider sharpness INCOMPLETE：bias 表达式涉及 conditioning on misclassified Z，\\n产生 E[Y|X,Z*] = Σ_z P(Z=z|Z*) E[Y|X,Z=z]。\\n对 C 做 supremum 要求联合优化 P(Z=z|Z*)，subject to C 为 valid confusion matrix，\\n产生非凸 bilinear 约束。数值优化达到 analytical bound 的 93%，强烈暗示 sharpness，\\n但形式化证明 supremum is attained 被 feasible set 的非凸拓扑阻断。\\n\\nCoverage 略低于 nominal（average 91.3% at 95% nominal）因为 ASV bounds 在已知 exact C 下推导，\\n而 MC 用的是有限样本估计的 C。Gap（3.7%）反映估计不确定性而非 bound failure。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ASV MC Validation for M-bias, Instrument, Front-door\",\n    \"description\": \"推导剩余 3 个拓扑的 ASV 表达式 + MC 验证。\\nMonotonicity 和 coverage 验证。Sharpness 作为 conjectures + numerical evidence。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"monotonicity_holds\": [\n        \"M-bias\",\n        \"instrument\",\n        \"front-door\"\n      ],\n      \"monotonicity_failures\": 0,\n      \"sharpness_numerical\": {\n        \"mbias\": \"achieving 92% of bound\",\n        \"instrument\": \"achieving 89% of bound\",\n        \"frontdoor\": \"achieving 94% of bound\"\n      },\n      \"coverage_at_95_nominal\": {\n        \"mbias\": 0.9,\n        \"instrument\": 0.89,\n        \"frontdoor\": 0.91\n      },\n      \"instrument_conservatism\": \"ASV bounds 1.8× wider than necessary\",\n      \"total_asv_coverage_6_topologies\": 0.907\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"ASV Results for Secondary Topologies\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"topology\",\n          \"monotonicity\",\n          \"sharpness_numerical_pct\",\n          \"coverage_95\",\n          \"conservatism\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"M-bias\",\n            \"holds\",\n            \"92%\",\n            0.9,\n            \"comparable to collider\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"instrument\",\n            \"holds\",\n            \"89%\",\n            0.89,\n            \"1.8× conservative (Wald ratio)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"front-door\",\n            \"holds\",\n            \"94%\",\n            0.91,\n            \"near-tight\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"All 6 Topologies ASV Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"topology\",\n          \"monotonicity\",\n          \"sharpness_status\",\n          \"coverage_95\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"confounding\",\n            \"proved\",\n            \"proved (formal)\",\n            0.93\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mediation\",\n            \"proved\",\n            \"proved (formal)\",\n            0.9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"collider\",\n            \"proved\",\n            \"93% numerical\",\n            0.91\n          ],\n          [\n            \"M-bias\",\n            \"proved\",\n            \"92% numerical\",\n            0.9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"instrument\",\n            \"proved\",\n            \"89% numerical\",\n            0.89\n          ],\n          [\n            \"front-door\",\n            \"proved\",\n            \"94% numerical\",\n            0.91\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"6 个拓扑全部有 ASV 表达式 + validated monotonicity。Sharpness landscape：\\n2 proved (confounding, mediation) + 4 numerical (collider 93%, front-door 94%, M-bias 92%, instrument 89%)。\\nInstrument 是最弱环节——ASV 保守性限制了实用性。论文应诚实讨论并标记 tighter instrument-specific bounds 为 future work。\\nOverall average 95%-nominal coverage = 0.907，在 median 档 [0.88, 0.93] 范围内。\\n\\n\\nMonotonicity 对所有 3 个拓扑成立——与 plan_004 相同的结构性论证：\\nASV 是 minimum-over-perturbation 量，在 perturbation budget δ 中固有单调。\\n\\nSharpness numerical evidence 有差异：front-door 最接近 tight（94%，identification structure 较简单），\\nM-bias 中等（92%），instrument 最远（89%）。\\nInstrument gap 反映 Wald estimator 的 ratio structure——supremum 涉及优化 misclassified 量的 ratio，\\nlandscape 有多个 local optima。\\n\\nInstrument ASV 显著保守（1.8× wider）因为 Wald estimator 放大小分母扰动，\\nworst-case bound 比 typical case 差很多。这是 IV sensitivity analysis 的已知问题（非本框架特有）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ASV Calibration on Empirical Data\",\n    \"description\": \"将 ASVs 应用于 plan_003 的经验 confusion matrices，跨 3 CSS tasks × 3 LLMs。\\n在 held-out gold-standard splits 上验证 coverage。\\n比较 ASV 可解释性与 raw confusion matrix reporting。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_scenarios\": 9,\n      \"empirical_asv_concordance\": 7,\n      \"concordance_failures\": 2,\n      \"failure_scenarios\": [\n        \"toxicity-Llama4 vs toxicity-Qwen35\",\n        \"toxicity-Qwen35 vs toxicity-DeepSeek\"\n      ],\n      \"failure_reason\": \"all 3 models produce high ASVs (>2.0) for toxicity K=2; differences within estimation noise\",\n      \"asv_ranking\": {\n        \"protest\": \"DeepSeek (0.91) > Llama4 (0.82) > Qwen35 (0.68) — correct\",\n        \"stance\": \"DeepSeek (1.41) > Llama4 (1.24) > Qwen35 (1.08) — correct\",\n        \"toxicity\": \"DeepSeek (2.44) ≈ Llama4 (2.31) ≈ Qwen35 (2.18) — indistinguishable\"\n      },\n      \"held_out_coverage_95\": 0.89\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"ASV Values and Concordance by Task × Model\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"task\",\n          \"model\",\n          \"ASV_95\",\n          \"observed_abs_bias\",\n          \"robust_flag\",\n          \"concordant\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"protest\",\n            \"Llama 4\",\n            0.82,\n            0.09,\n            \"moderate\",\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"protest\",\n            \"Qwen 3.5\",\n            0.68,\n            0.12,\n            \"fragile\",\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"protest\",\n            \"DeepSeek\",\n            0.91,\n            0.05,\n            \"moderate-high\",\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"stance\",\n            \"Llama 4\",\n            1.24,\n            0.06,\n            \"moderate-high\",\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"stance\",\n            \"Qwen 3.5\",\n            1.08,\n            0.08,\n            \"moderate\",\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"stance\",\n            \"DeepSeek\",\n            1.41,\n            0.03,\n            \"high\",\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"toxicity\",\n            \"Llama 4\",\n            2.31,\n            0.02,\n            \"high\",\n            true\n          ],\n          [\n            \"toxicity\",\n            \"Qwen 3.5\",\n            2.18,\n            0.04,\n            \"high\",\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"toxicity\",\n            \"DeepSeek\",\n            2.44,\n            0.01,\n            \"high\",\n            false\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ASVs 在 moderate-to-high bias scenarios 中具有经验实用性（protest K=5, stance K=3），\\n但在 low-bias regime 失去区分力（toxicity K=2）。这是诚实且预期的——\\n类似 E-values 在 confounding 小时不 informative。\\n论文应 frame 为：\\\"ASVs are most valuable when annotation error is non-trivial (K≥3, accuracy <0.85)——\\nprecisely the scenarios where researchers lack existing diagnostic tools。\\\"\\n7/9 concordance 支持 Claim 2 的实用价值。\\n\\n\\nConcordance 7/9：ASV 在 protest (K=5) 和 stance (K=3) 任务上正确排序模型鲁棒性——\\n这些任务的 confusion matrix 差异足够大，产生有区分力的 ASV 值。\\nFailure 出现在 toxicity (K=2)：所有 3 个模型有 near-diagonal C（accuracy > 0.86），\\n产生高 ASVs (>2.0)，差异在 MC estimation noise 内——无法区分模型。\\n\\n这是 low-bias regime 的结构性限制：annotation quality 高时（K=2 toxicity），\\nASVs 正确指示\\\"robust\\\"但不能 rank-order models。\\n这实际上是合适的——如果所有模型产生 negligible bias，ranking 本身就无信息量。\\n\\nHeld-out coverage (0.89 at 95% nominal) 略低于 MC coverage (0.91) 因为 empirical C 有额外的\\ngold-standard sample size 估计噪声。Gap 小且在预期范围内。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Correction Guidance Framework: Decision Mapping and Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Decision framework: {topology × error structure × ASV} → correction method\\n(DSL / PPI / MLA / naive plug-in / \\\"no existing method adequate\\\")。\\nMC validation: 90 scenarios + empirical validation on plan_003 data。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_mc_scenarios\": 90,\n      \"correction_framework_accuracy\": 0.89,\n      \"correct_recommendations\": 80,\n      \"boundary_indistinguishable_cases\": 3,\n      \"hard_failure_cases\": 7,\n      \"failure_breakdown\": {\n        \"near_diagonal_all_methods_equivalent\": 3,\n        \"differential_intermediate_mismatch\": 2,\n        \"false_recommendation_in_hopeless_regime\": 2\n      },\n      \"method_dominance\": {\n        \"DSL\": \"best in 28/90 (diagonal-dominant C, confounding/mediation)\",\n        \"PPI\": \"best in 22/90 (moderate C, exposure/front-door)\",\n        \"MLA\": \"best in 18/90 (high off-diagonal, confounding/collider)\",\n        \"naive_plugin\": \"best in 12/90 (near-diagonal, any topology)\",\n        \"no_method_adequate\": \"10/90 (near-permutation + reversal topologies)\"\n      },\n      \"empirical_validation_plan003\": {\n        \"protest_correct\": true,\n        \"stance_correct\": true,\n        \"toxicity_correct\": true\n      },\n      \"open_problems\": [\n        \"dependence-aware multi-LLM correction\",\n        \"differential K≥3 error correction\",\n        \"collider + near-permutation C (no method reduces bias below 50%)\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Correction Method Dominance Map\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"best_in_n\",\n          \"primary_topology\",\n          \"primary_error_regime\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DSL\",\n            28,\n            \"confounding, mediation\",\n            \"diagonal-dominant C\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"PPI\",\n            22,\n            \"exposure, front-door\",\n            \"moderate off-diagonal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MLA\",\n            18,\n            \"confounding, collider\",\n            \"high off-diagonal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"naive plug-in\",\n            12,\n            \"any\",\n            \"near-diagonal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"no method\",\n            10,\n            \"exposure, mediation\",\n            \"near-permutation\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Framework Failure Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"failure_type\",\n          \"count\",\n          \"impact\",\n          \"mitigation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"boundary (methods ≤5% apart)\",\n            3,\n            \"low\",\n            \"any recommendation acceptable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"differential mismatch\",\n            2,\n            \"moderate\",\n            \"add continuous differentiality parameter\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"false recommendation in hopeless regime\",\n            2,\n            \"high\",\n            \"add safety check: if reversal topology + extreme C → flag\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Correction framework 达到主要目标：89% 正确识别 best correction method。\\n11% failure rate 集中在固有歧义的 boundary cases（3%）和真正困难的 regimes（8%）。\\n2 个\\\"false recommendation in hopeless regime\\\"最令人担忧——框架提供了虚假信心。\\n论文应明确讨论此风险并建议 practitioners 始终在 held-out data 上验证 corrections。\\n10 个\\\"no method adequate\\\"scenarios 是论文对 open problems 的贡献——\\n特别是 dependence-aware multi-LLM correction（结合 plan_003 的 correlation 发现）。\\n\\n\\n89% accuracy 反映框架在 clear-cut scenarios（方法性能明显分离）的优势和 boundary cases 的弱点。\\n\\n3 个 boundary cases 是结构性不可区分的：near-diagonal C（low error）下所有方法结果相近（within 5%），\\n\\\"best\\\" recommendation 是任意的。这不是框架的失败而是问题本身的 degeneracy。\\n\\n7 个 hard failures：\\n(a) 3 cases: near-diagonal C 使所有方法等效但框架因 threshold effects 选了次优方法；\\n(b) 2 cases: intermediate differential error 处框架的 non-differential/differential 二分类\\n无法捕获 differentiality 的连续性质；\\n(c) 2 cases: 框架推荐了方法但正确答案是\\\"no method adequate\\\"（near-permutation C + reversal topology）。\\n\\nMethod dominance 是 topology-driven 的：DSL 擅长 confounding（调整 misclassified confounder 是其 native use case），\\nPPI 擅长 exposure（regression-calibration 处理 treatment misclassification），\\nMLA 擅长 high off-diagonal error（maximum likelihood 直接建模 C）。\\n\\n10/90 \\\"no method adequate\\\" 集中在 reversal topologies（exposure, mediation）+ extreme C——\\n这些是 current correction literature 的真实 gaps。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Pathological Confusion Matrix Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"极端 C 结构分析：near-permutation, rank-deficient, block-diagonal。\\n刻画 catastrophic bias 条件并识别结构性预测因子。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"spectral_gap_predictive_R2\": 0.78,\n      \"diagonal_dominance_predictive_R2\": 0.71,\n      \"combined_predictor_R2\": 0.84,\n      \"catastrophic_threshold_spectral_gap\": 0.3,\n      \"catastrophic_threshold_diagonal_dominance\": 0.5,\n      \"near_permutation_universally_catastrophic\": true,\n      \"rank_deficient_topology_dependent\": true,\n      \"rank_deficient_worst\": [\n        \"front-door\",\n        \"instrument\"\n      ],\n      \"block_diagonal_worst\": \"mediation (blocks indirect path)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Structural Predictors of Bias Severity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"predictor\",\n          \"R2_overall\",\n          \"best_topology_R2\",\n          \"worst_topology_R2\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"spectral gap\",\n            0.78,\n            \"exposure (0.85)\",\n            \"M-bias (0.67)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"diagonal dominance\",\n            0.71,\n            \"confounding (0.82)\",\n            \"front-door (0.58)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"spectral gap + diag dom\",\n            0.84,\n            \"exposure (0.91)\",\n            \"instrument (0.74)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Catastrophic Bias Conditions by Topology and C Structure\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"topology\",\n          \"near_permutation\",\n          \"rank_deficient\",\n          \"block_diagonal\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"confounding\",\n            \"severe (OVB > 2×)\",\n            \"moderate\",\n            \"moderate\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"exposure\",\n            \"catastrophic (reversal)\",\n            \"severe\",\n            \"severe (block reversal)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mediation\",\n            \"severe (reversal)\",\n            \"moderate\",\n            \"severe (block indirect effects)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"collider\",\n            \"severe (attenuation > 60%)\",\n            \"moderate\",\n            \"moderate\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"M-bias\",\n            \"moderate\",\n            \"moderate\",\n            \"mild\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"instrument\",\n            \"moderate\",\n            \"catastrophic (Wald denom → 0)\",\n            \"moderate\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"front-door\",\n            \"moderate\",\n            \"catastrophic (identification loss)\",\n            \"moderate\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"实用 takeaway：spectral gap < 0.3 OR diagonal dominance < 0.5 → 所有拓扑均高风险。\\n这一双阈值规则足够简单可用且捕获 84% 的 bias variance。\\nFront-door 和 instrument 对 rank-deficient C 特别脆弱（ratio estimator 分母问题）。\\n这些 structural predictors 是 toolkit (plan_010) 的 automatic diagnostic features 候选。\\n\\n\\nSpectral gap（C 的第一和第二 eigenvalue 之差）预测 bias severity（R²=0.78）\\n因为它捕获了 C 距 permutation matrix 的距离——反转的结构性来源。\\nR²=0.78 表示强但不完美的预测；剩余方差来自 topology-specific interactions。\\n\\nDiagonal dominance（minimum diagonal element）是更简单的 proxy，R² 略低（0.71）。\\nCombined spectral gap + diagonal dominance 达到 R²=0.84——两个 features 捕获了大部分 bias-relevant C structure。\\n\\nNear-permutation 普遍 catastrophic 因为 label-swapping 搅乱所有拓扑。\\nRank-deficient C 是 topology-dependent：front-door 和 instrument 的 identification formula\\n含有 C-dependent 分母——C rank-deficient 时分母趋零，bias unbounded。\\nConfounding/mediation/collider 对 rank deficiency 处理更 graceful（无 ratio estimator）。\\n\\nBlock-diagonal C 对 mediation 最 severe——block 结构可以创造 artifact category boundaries 上的 apparent indirect effects。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"annot-sensitivity Python Toolkit\",\n    \"description\": \"Open-source pip-installable package：user-specified DAG + confusion matrix + downstream estimate\\n→ bias expressions + ASV + sensitivity curves + correction recommendation + diagnostic plots。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"package_name\": \"annot-sensitivity\",\n      \"supported_topologies\": 6,\n      \"supported_K_range\": \"2–10\",\n      \"core_api\": [\n        \"compute_bias(dag, C, estimate) → BiasResult\",\n        \"compute_asv(dag, C, estimate, delta_range) → ASVResult\",\n        \"recommend_correction(dag, C, asv) → CorrectionRecommendation\",\n        \"diagnostic_plot(result) → Figure\",\n        \"eigendecomp_summary(C, K) → EigenSummary\",\n        \"check_pathological(C) → PathologyReport (spectral gap + diag dom thresholds)\"\n      ],\n      \"worked_examples\": 3,\n      \"example_topologies\": [\n        \"confounding (baseline)\",\n        \"exposure (reversal)\",\n        \"mediation (conditional reversal)\"\n      ],\n      \"test_coverage\": 0.87,\n      \"documentation\": \"API reference + 3 tutorial notebooks + quick-start guide\",\n      \"known_limitations\": [\n        \"K>7 eigendecomposition slow (>10s/computation)\",\n        \"correction accuracy inherits plan_007 limitations (89%)\",\n        \"CLI + notebook only, no GUI\",\n        \"3/6 topologies lack detailed tutorials (M-bias, instrument, front-door)\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Toolkit 是 functional deliverable，使论文的理论贡献对 practitioners 可及。\\n3 个 worked examples 覆盖最重要的场景（reversal cases）。\\n主要 gap：3 个拓扑缺少 tutorial，可能限制 M-bias/instrument/front-door 用户的采纳。\\nPost-publication 低成本 follow-up。\\n\\n3 个 worked examples（而非 6）因为 median 档 scope 有限——优先覆盖 3 个 reversal-relevant 拓扑\\n（confounding 作为 baseline，exposure + mediation 作为反转案例）。剩余 3 个拓扑在 API 中支持但缺少详细 tutorial。\\n\\nK>7 性能限制反映 eigendecomposition 的 O(K³) 成本——对典型 CSS 使用（K=3–7）可接受，\\n对罕见 high-K 应用偏慢。\\n\\nTest coverage 0.87 反映核心计算（bias expressions, ASV）的 thorough unit testing\\n和 visualization/correction recommendation 组件的 lighter testing。\\n\\ncheck_pathological() 集成 plan_009 的 spectral gap + diagonal dominance 阈值，\\n为 practitioner 提供自动 C matrix 质量诊断。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1237,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1237}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G63BGcBSV4o7q4UjTXE76r","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — causal_annot_error_attrib\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: AAAI 2027 (abstract: 2026-07-21, paper: 2026-07-28)\n5\t- Secondary: ARR October 2026 (~2026-10-15, commit to NAACL 2027 / ACL 2027)\n6\t- Tertiary: ICWSM 2027 Round 2 (2026-09-15)\n7\t\n8\t## Title\n9\tMulti-Class Annotation Errors Are Not Created Equal: Bias Taxonomy, Sensitivity Analysis, and Correction Guidance for LLM-Annotated Causal Studies\n10\t\n11\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n12\t\n13\t1. **Multi-class bias taxonomy**: For K≥3 annotation variables, the direction and magnitude of downstream bias depend on the interaction between the K×K confusion matrix structure and the DAG topology — breaking guarantees that hold in the binary case. We provide closed-form bias expressions for K=3 and matrix-form expressions with interpretability tools for general K, across 6 canonical social-science DAG topologies (confounding, mediation, collider, M-bias, instrument, front-door).\n14\t\n15\t2. **Annotation Sensitivity Values (ASVs)**: A sensitivity analysis framework for annotation-induced bias. ASVs quantify the minimum degree of differential annotation error needed to overturn a downstream conclusion, parameterized by a reference confusion matrix and amplification factor δ. Reported alongside estimates, analogous to E-values for unmeasured confounding. Formal proofs (monotonicity + sharpness) for 3 priority topologies; MC-validated conjectures for the remaining 3.\n16\t\n17\t3. **Correction guidance framework**: A principled decision framework mapping {DAG topology × error structure × ASV} to the appropriate correction method (DSL, PPI, MLA, naive plug-in), characterizing regimes where each applies and where no existing method suffices — including dependence-aware multi-LLM correction as an open problem.\n18\t\n19\t## Story Spine\n20\t\n21\t- **Problem**: LLMs are rapidly replacing human annotators in CSS, but Baumann et al. (2025) show 31% of downstream conclusions are already incorrect. Researchers lack diagnostic tools to answer: (a) which annotation error structures propagate bias under their causal design, and (b) how robust their conclusions are to annotation error. Kim et al. (ICML 2025) show cross-model errors are highly correlated (60% agreement when both err), meaning ensembles cannot escape systematic bias — researchers MUST analyze the error structure of their chosen annotator, which is exactly what our tools enable.\n22\t\n23\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Wood-Doughty et al. (2018) apply DAG reasoning to text classifier errors but produce no formal bias theorems (binary only). TeBlunthuis et al. (2024) provide the most complete binary treatment with MLA correction but are limited to K=2, single classifier. Lee & Wood-Doughty (2024) extend to categorical + LLM classifiers but cover only 1 DAG topology (unobserved confounding), with no systematic taxonomy or sensitivity analysis. VanderWeele & Li (2019) provide sensitivity bounds but only for binary risk ratios. Jerzak et al. (EMNLP 2025) benchmark correction methods but treat error as monolithic — if different confusion matrix structures produce qualitatively different bias in different DAG topologies, unconditional benchmarking is itself misleading.\n24\t\n25\t- **Our framing**: Multi-class annotation errors are not created equal. The same confusion matrix that produces innocuous residual bias in one DAG topology can produce direction-reversing toxic bias in another. We provide the first systematic characterization of this interaction (the taxonomy), a tool to quantify robustness (ASVs), and guidance for when/how to correct (the framework). This is not a new correction method — it is the missing diagnostic layer that tells researchers which correction is appropriate, or whether correction is needed at all.\n26\t\n27\t- **Headline result template**: \"Across 6 DAG topologies with K=3,5,7, our bias expressions correctly predict bias direction and magnitude within 95% MC confidence intervals. On 3 CSS tasks annotated by 3 LLMs, ASVs provide calibrated robustness indicators, and our taxonomy identifies cases where commonly applied corrections would increase rather than decrease bias.\"\n28\t\n29\t## Core Insight (Lead Finding) — DUAL VERSION, gate on plan_001\n30\t\n31\t### Version A (≥1 topology shows direction reversal under K≥3 non-differential exposure misclassification)\n32\tThe binary guarantee that \"non-differential exposure misclassification biases toward the null\" (Bross 1954) breaks in the multi-class case. For specific confusion matrix structures in specific DAG topologies, K≥3 non-differential error can amplify or reverse effect estimates. Brenner (1993) identified this possibility for polytomous confounder misclassification (\"bias can go in either direction\"); we provide the first systematic characterization across 6 DAG topologies with exact conditions for each {C structure × topology} cell. Furthermore, binarizing a K-class variable to \"escape\" into the binary regime is itself hazardous — collapsing introduces new, direction-unpredictable bias (MVP evidence: Δ up to 0.103).\n33\t\n34\t### Version B (no direction reversal found across topologies)\n35\tMulti-class annotation error is structurally irreducible to the binary case: the downstream bias magnitude depends on the full K×K confusion matrix in ways that binary sensitivity/specificity cannot predict, and binarizing a K-class variable introduces new bias (MVP evidence: Δ up to 0.103). While non-differential error preserves bias direction across tested topologies (a useful practitioners' guarantee), the magnitude varies dramatically with confusion matrix structure (0.13–0.30 in confounding DAG alone), and this variation is topology-dependent. ASVs provide the missing robustness measure for this quantitative — not directional — uncertainty.\n36\t\n37\t**Gate**: plan_001 results determine which version. ≥2 topologies with reversal → A; 1 → A with that topology as lead; 0 → B. See D003.\n38\t\n39\t## MVP Evidence\n40\t\n41\t**Confounding DAG + K=3** (confounder misclassification):\n42\t- Theoretical bias expressions match MC perfectly (6/6 structures within 95% CI) — framework validated\n43\t- Binary collapse ≠ multi-class: Δ up to 0.103 (near-permutation C), proving K=3 retains more confounding control than binarization\n44\t- 100k random C search: confounding DAG bias is monotonically toward OVB — this topology is \"well-behaved\" (predictable direction)\n45\t- NOTE: Confounding DAG tests residual confounding, NOT bias-toward-null (Bross 1954). Criterion 2 (away-from-null bias) holds for binary too in this topology. See M001.\n46\t\n47\t**Exposure DAG K=3** (exposure misclassification — D002/D004 CONFIRMED):\n48\t- 100k random C: 85% violate bias-toward-null, 83.4% sign reversal, 14.1% amplification\n49\t- K=2 control: 6/6 toward null (binary guarantee holds)\n50\t- Worst case: β=1.0 → estimate=-0.84 (sign reversal + 2.83x amplification)\n51\t- Mechanism: near-permutation C causes label swap → effect direction flips (structurally impossible in K=2)\n52\t- **Two-DAG contrast**: confounding (monotonic, predictable) vs exposure (unpredictable, topology-dependent) — validates core claim\n53\t\n54\t## Venue Fit Risks\n55\t\n56\t- **AAAI**: Broad AI audience — emphasize general methodology for \"automated annotation measurement error,\" not LLM-specific. Frame as extending classical measurement error theory to modern automated labeling.\n57\t- **ARR/NAACL**: NLP audience — CSS track is natural fit. May want more empirical NLP experiments. Balance theory with practical LLM annotation scenarios.\n58\t- **Cross-discipline bridge**: Epidemiology (measurement error theory) × NLP (annotation errors). Epi reviewers check proof rigor; NLP reviewers check empirical relevance. Must serve both.\n59\t\n60\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Planned Responses\n61\t\n62\t1. **\"Trivial extension of binary to multi-class\"** → Brenner (1993) proved direction reversal; our taxonomy provides the first systematic characterization across 6 topologies. Binarizing K-class introduces NEW unpredictable bias (MVP evidence). The complexity jump is structural: binary has 2 free parameters (sensitivity, specificity) → scalar bias; K=5 has 20 free parameters → matrix-valued bias requiring eigendecomposition for interpretation. [Experiments: plan_001, plan_008]\n63\t\n64\t2. **\"Lee & Wood-Doughty (2024) already did categorical\"** → They cover 1 topology (unobserved confounding) on 1 dataset (MIMIC). We cover 6 topologies with systematic taxonomy + ASVs + correction guidance. Their work is a stepping stone; ours is the full framework. [Experiments: plan_001]\n65\t\n66\t3. **\"Why these 6 DAG topologies?\"** → These are the canonical CSS causal designs used by Hernán & Cole (2009) and TeBlunthuis et al. (2024). They cover the major roles an annotated variable can play: confounder, mediator, collider, instrument, front-door criterion variable. [Experiments: plan_001]\n67\t\n68\t4. **\"K≥5 expressions aren't actionable\"** → Three interpretability tools: (a) eigendecomposition summaries identifying dominant bias modes, (b) worst-case scalar bounds, (c) diagnostic visualizations. [Experiments: plan_002]\n69\t\n70\t5. **\"ASV sharpness only proved for 3 topologies\"** → Honest scoping reflecting algebraic complexity. Remaining 3 validated via MC with numerical sharpness evidence. Full proofs identified as immediate future work. [Experiments: plan_004, plan_005]\n71\t\n72\t6. **\"Correlated multi-LLM errors?\"** → Kim et al. (ICML 2025) actually STRENGTHENS our case: if ensembles can't fix errors (60% agreement when both err), error structure analysis is the only viable approach. Multi-annotator correction with dependence is identified as an open problem. [Framework discussion]\n73\t\n74\t7. **\"Empirical validation scope\"** → 3 CSS tasks × 3 LLMs × 3 DAG-relevant scenarios. Tasks selected to cover K=2,3,5 annotation complexity. [Experiments: plan_003, plan_006]\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25bf0861-1839-4453-8613-912d152b4cb0","uuid":"054fae7b-db34-47c5-acb4-bf6f454264ec","timestamp":"2026-05-20T08:29:41.698Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-prod_0510/projects/causal_annot_error_attrib/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T074549/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — causal_annot_error_attrib\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: AAAI 2027 (abstract: 2026-07-21, paper: 2026-07-28)\n- Secondary: ARR October 2026 (~2026-10-15, commit to NAACL 2027 / ACL 2027)\n- Tertiary: ICWSM 2027 Round 2 (2026-09-15)\n\n## Title\nMulti-Class Annotation Errors Are Not Created Equal: Bias Taxonomy, Sensitivity Analysis, and Correction Guidance for LLM-Annotated Causal Studies\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n1. **Multi-class bias taxonomy**: For K≥3 annotation variables, the direction and magnitude of downstream bias depend on the interaction between the K×K confusion matrix structure and the DAG topology — breaking guarantees that hold in the binary case. We provide closed-form bias expressions for K=3 and matrix-form expressions with interpretability tools for general K, across 6 canonical social-science DAG topologies (confounding, mediation, collider, M-bias, instrument, front-door).\n\n2. **Annotation Sensitivity Values (ASVs)**: A sensitivity analysis framework for annotation-induced bias. ASVs quantify the minimum degree of differential annotation error needed to overturn a downstream conclusion, parameterized by a reference confusion matrix and amplification factor δ. Reported alongside estimates, analogous to E-values for unmeasured confounding. Formal proofs (monotonicity + sharpness) for 3 priority topologies; MC-validated conjectures for the remaining 3.\n\n3. **Correction guidance framework**: A principled decision framework mapping {DAG topology × error structure × ASV} to the appropriate correction method (DSL, PPI, MLA, naive plug-in), characterizing regimes where each applies and where no existing method suffices — including dependence-aware multi-LLM correction as an open problem.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: LLMs are rapidly replacing human annotators in CSS, but Baumann et al. (2025) show 31% of downstream conclusions are already incorrect. Researchers lack diagnostic tools to answer: (a) which annotation error structures propagate bias under their causal design, and (b) how robust their conclusions are to annotation error. Kim et al. (ICML 2025) show cross-model errors are highly correlated (60% agreement when both err), meaning ensembles cannot escape systematic bias — researchers MUST analyze the error structure of their chosen annotator, which is exactly what our tools enable.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Wood-Doughty et al. (2018) apply DAG reasoning to text classifier errors but produce no formal bias theorems (binary only). TeBlunthuis et al. (2024) provide the most complete binary treatment with MLA correction but are limited to K=2, single classifier. Lee & Wood-Doughty (2024) extend to categorical + LLM classifiers but cover only 1 DAG topology (unobserved confounding), with no systematic taxonomy or sensitivity analysis. VanderWeele & Li (2019) provide sensitivity bounds but only for binary risk ratios. Jerzak et al. (EMNLP 2025) benchmark correction methods but treat error as monolithic — if different confusion matrix structures produce qualitatively different bias in different DAG topologies, unconditional benchmarking is itself misleading.\n\n- **Our framing**: Multi-class annotation errors are not created equal. The same confusion matrix that produces innocuous residual bias in one DAG topology can produce direction-reversing toxic bias in another. We provide the first systematic characterization of this interaction (the taxonomy), a tool to quantify robustness (ASVs), and guidance for when/how to correct (the framework). This is not a new correction method — it is the missing diagnostic layer that tells researchers which correction is appropriate, or whether correction is needed at all.\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"Across 6 DAG topologies with K=3,5,7, our bias expressions correctly predict bias direction and magnitude within 95% MC confidence intervals. On 3 CSS tasks annotated by 3 LLMs, ASVs provide calibrated robustness indicators, and our taxonomy identifies cases where commonly applied corrections would increase rather than decrease bias.\"\n\n## Core Insight (Lead Finding) — DUAL VERSION, gate on plan_001\n\n### Version A (≥1 topology shows direction reversal under K≥3 non-differential exposure misclassification)\nThe binary guarantee that \"non-differential exposure misclassification biases toward the null\" (Bross 1954) breaks in the multi-class case. For specific confusion matrix structures in specific DAG topologies, K≥3 non-differential error can amplify or reverse effect estimates. Brenner (1993) identified this possibility for polytomous confounder misclassification (\"bias can go in either direction\"); we provide the first systematic characterization across 6 DAG topologies with exact conditions for each {C structure × topology} cell. Furthermore, binarizing a K-class variable to \"escape\" into the binary regime is itself hazardous — collapsing introduces new, direction-unpredictable bias (MVP evidence: Δ up to 0.103).\n\n### Version B (no direction reversal found across topologies)\nMulti-class annotation error is structurally irreducible to the binary case: the downstream bias magnitude depends on the full K×K confusion matrix in ways that binary sensitivity/specificity cannot predict, and binarizing a K-class variable introduces new bias (MVP evidence: Δ up to 0.103). While non-differential error preserves bias direction across tested topologies (a useful practitioners' guarantee), the magnitude varies dramatically with confusion matrix structure (0.13–0.30 in confounding DAG alone), and this variation is topology-dependent. ASVs provide the missing robustness measure for this quantitative — not directional — uncertainty.\n\n**Gate**: plan_001 results determine which version. ≥2 topologies with reversal → A; 1 → A with that topology as lead; 0 → B. See D003.\n\n## MVP Evidence\n\n**Confounding DAG + K=3** (confounder misclassification):\n- Theoretical bias expressions match MC perfectly (6/6 structures within 95% CI) — framework validated\n- Binary collapse ≠ multi-class: Δ up to 0.103 (near-permutation C), proving K=3 retains more confounding control than binarization\n- 100k random C search: confounding DAG bias is monotonically toward OVB — this topology is \"well-behaved\" (predictable direction)\n- NOTE: Confounding DAG tests residual confounding, NOT bias-toward-null (Bross 1954). Criterion 2 (away-from-null bias) holds for binary too in this topology. See M001.\n\n**Exposure DAG K=3** (exposure misclassification — D002/D004 CONFIRMED):\n- 100k random C: 85% violate bias-toward-null, 83.4% sign reversal, 14.1% amplification\n- K=2 control: 6/6 toward null (binary guarantee holds)\n- Worst case: β=1.0 → estimate=-0.84 (sign reversal + 2.83x amplification)\n- Mechanism: near-permutation C causes label swap → effect direction flips (structurally impossible in K=2)\n- **Two-DAG contrast**: confounding (monotonic, predictable) vs exposure (unpredictable, topology-dependent) — validates core claim\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **AAAI**: Broad AI audience — emphasize general methodology for \"automated annotation measurement error,\" not LLM-specific. Frame as extending classical measurement error theory to modern automated labeling.\n- **ARR/NAACL**: NLP audience — CSS track is natural fit. May want more empirical NLP experiments. Balance theory with practical LLM annotation scenarios.\n- **Cross-discipline bridge**: Epidemiology (measurement error theory) × NLP (annotation errors). Epi reviewers check proof rigor; NLP reviewers check empirical relevance. Must serve both.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Planned Responses\n\n1. **\"Trivial extension of binary to multi-class\"** → Brenner (1993) proved direction reversal; our taxonomy provides the first systematic characterization across 6 topologies. Binarizing K-class introduces NEW unpredictable bias (MVP evidence). The complexity jump is structural: binary has 2 free parameters (sensitivity, specificity) → scalar bias; K=5 has 20 free parameters → matrix-valued bias requiring eigendecomposition for interpretation. [Experiments: plan_001, plan_008]\n\n2. **\"Lee & Wood-Doughty (2024) already did categorical\"** → They cover 1 topology (unobserved confounding) on 1 dataset (MIMIC). We cover 6 topologies with systematic taxonomy + ASVs + correction guidance. Their work is a stepping stone; ours is the full framework. [Experiments: plan_001]\n\n3. **\"Why these 6 DAG topologies?\"** → These are the canonical CSS causal designs used by Hernán & Cole (2009) and TeBlunthuis et al. (2024). They cover the major roles an annotated variable can play: confounder, mediator, collider, instrument, front-door criterion variable. [Experiments: plan_001]\n\n4. **\"K≥5 expressions aren't actionable\"** → Three interpretability tools: (a) eigendecomposition summaries identifying dominant bias modes, (b) worst-case scalar bounds, (c) diagnostic visualizations. [Experiments: plan_002]\n\n5. **\"ASV sharpness only proved for 3 topologies\"** → Honest scoping reflecting algebraic complexity. Remaining 3 validated via MC with numerical sharpness evidence. Full proofs identified as immediate future work. [Experiments: plan_004, plan_005]\n\n6. **\"Correlated multi-LLM errors?\"** → Kim et al. (ICML 2025) actually STRENGTHENS our case: if ensembles can't fix errors (60% agreement when both err), error structure analysis is the only viable approach. Multi-annotator correction with dependence is identified as an open problem. [Framework discussion]\n\n7. **\"Empirical validation scope\"** → 3 CSS tasks × 3 LLMs × 3 DAG-relevant scenarios. Tasks selected to cover K=2,3,5 annotation complexity. [Experiments: plan_003, plan_006]\n","numLines":75,"startLine":1,"totalLines":75}}}
